115	2	5	To formalize the\ndesiredfunctionality,theinitiativehasadoptedthefollowingkeyattributes:economic,standardized,installed,reliable,\nandunattended[21].Eachoftheseattributesisexpectedtorequiredifferentlevelsofautomationinreactoroperations.\nThe current NRC guidelines for automation in reactor operations, as provided in Section 9 of NUREG-0700, are\nrootedinseveralfundamentalhumanfactorsengineeringconcepts:safety,resilience,performance,andthecapacityfor\nroot-causeanalysis.Theseconceptsarewellrepresentedandremainfundamentaltothesafeoperationandsuccessful\ndeployment of U.S. domestic nuclear reactor technologies. However, we find that if only these factors are considered,\nthe current guidelines on automation levels do not align with the long-term economic and commercial goals of the\nadvanced reactor community—particularly in regard to the operational characteristics of FBs [22, 21].	1. Introduction	72	2	\N	\N	{}	[-0.029470997,-0.080424495,-0.048460912,0.046030726,-0.01320415,0.020846456,-0.038984552,0.108533725,-0.13837819,-0.0035799185,-0.012133517,-0.04177544,0.09149641,0.0020935128,-0.051891357,-0.029011779,0.03026868,-0.101563916,-0.04075658,-0.059726287,0.0071912482,-0.016474687,0.042936377,0.0006035999,0.0057113846,-0.041721907,-0.0821019,-0.057273168,-0.027886773,-0.015668996,-0.018794263,-0.011327527,0.060175516,-0.06775114,0.06822399,0.0006542695,-0.014634095,0.0040357164,-0.0029083693,-0.031348653,-0.03765953,-0.12503769,-0.052290928,0.032804437,-0.080617316,0.051678043,-0.015769932,-0.11347661,-0.087295674,0.02697421,-0.0075274813,-0.039258532,0.047960136,0.05507162,0.11766723,-0.016277114,0.10947243,-0.09425934,0.0260226,0.055197854,0.009863106,-0.027749807,-0.022443084,-0.03641981,0.112178266,0.044923756,0.038295783,-0.082821,0.012985795,-0.035842,-0.00839796,-0.07196395,-0.017508734,0.011702181,0.01881664,-0.037336055,0.014985729,-0.015499394,0.056269217,-0.04779512,-0.04770207,0.0006705437,-0.0022197177,-0.051098924,-0.017207481,0.06672416,-0.065