249	3	39	This review\nexplores these dimensions, highlighting their implications for\nenergy industry stakeholders. Over -reliance on technology repre sents a significant risk, as\nincreased dependence on automated systems can lead to\nvulnerabilities when these systems fail or perform\nunpredictably. Automation, while minimizing human\nintervention, may lead to oversight errors or system failures. For examp le, the integration of inverter drives in industrial\nenergy systems enhances efficiency but also introduces risks\nof control failures and interference in operations (Leonowicz\n& Lempart, 2012) [22].	2. Literature Review	81	4	\N	\N	{}	[-0.070338696,0.038100135,0.044485845,0.055569936,0.029180333,-0.061031662,-0.016534513,0.06181802,-0.027420329,-0.008175584,-0.008522141,0.029741084,0.09498889,-0.07170758,-0.03526949,0.047163095,0.056015853,-0.12654047,-0.008893996,-0.050545305,-0.040355753,-0.04081619,-0.018356476,-0.014088296,-0.011125691,-0.03060357,-0.034083705,-0.023599183,-0.10463982,-0.00176144,-0.09185102,-0.07350305,-0.005294636,-0.03207517,0.0366845,0.035767894,0.04005222,0.028619746,0.076536275,-0.10033943,0.029890578,-0.135225,-0.038947698,-0.019374738,-0.020659756,-0.025358155,0.023078313,-0.09453594,0.02905933,-0.07553041,-0.020986227,-0.028955167,0.08476448,-0.07744803,0.016269328,-0.03055445,0.090802915,0.00568387,0.014876254,0.004563897,0.062242035,-0.05336118,-0.019627055,0.026026988,0.02116676,0.07913861,0.046224337,-0.020633038,-0.02522028,-0.028105041,-0.052591305,-0.048996992,-0.0066769766,-0.0050509986,0.027544085,-0.047740594,-0.02708699,-0.062380515,0.049422886,-0.073467344,0.053235047,-0.012798109,-0.07373766,0.03223083,0.029420689,0.028060954,0.049817983,-0.0017896864,0.11706104,0.0199599,-0.046424784,-0.08264076,0.08249418,0.07034015,0.11919139,0.048393704,0.05763305,-0.038879078,-0.054195777,-0.018808689,0.08933128,0.03338512,-0.032226212,-0.054658588,-0.058504175,-0.030489521,-0.040526893,0.013769581,0.06455848,-0.113860205,0.09953