280	3	70	By\nreducing human error and improving the precision of\nresponse mechanisms, autom ation contributes to safer and\nmore reliable operations across energy sectors (Vagaš et al.,\n2018) [35]. While the implementation of automation for safety in\nindustries such as energy presents a host of challenges,\nincluding technological costs, workforce skill gaps, and the\ntransition from manual to automated systems, it also offers\nsubstantial benefits. These benefits include improved\npredictive maintenance, faster incident response times, and\nenhanced safety by reducing human exposure to hazardous\ntasks.	2. Literature Review	84	3	\N	\N	{}	[-0.06641173,0.01285387,0.0033215608,0.053037897,0.023424856,-0.019206164,0.044651203,0.0725534,-0.07478882,0.04179661,-0.025778593,-0.043531734,0.022307226,-0.039583545,-0.028292052,-0.023635894,0.0991181,-0.06374452,-0.040949274,-0.09459584,-0.0005151589,0.031997718,0.014667805,0.05613616,-0.029849714,-0.022170754,-0.044280056,0.025448823,-0.040750146,-0.043585338,-0.032308586,-0.06488776,0.04487652,0.028121937,-0.028820781,-0.019868184,-0.05787461,0.0484232,0.006224439,-0.12513597,-0.033413168,-0.13565353,-0.016770825,-0.0072765485,-0.011255447,0.08460102,0.006538933,-0.11140433,0.033831555,-0.045163203,-0.041526537,0.062956676,0.0896655,-0.042058464,-0.052683387,0.038710937,0.06995541,-0.0072810594,-0.0891474,-0.031542026,0.019202918,-0.0957325,-0.08378927,-0.0016827185,0.02594573,0.02712869,0.061158776,-0.04519697,0.022752147,0.008244231,0.011623956,-0.06014373,0.0033752834,-0.0034616909,0.03339302,-0.047053095,-0.075319216,-0.047805037,0.08309624,-0.00023847356,0.0106195705,-0.04950166,0.008380963,0.07057142,0.030094342,0.054420885,0.021636885,0.06914195,0.056452222,0.0330368,-0.015631361,-0.04322634,0.082811214,0.034189243,0.038272645,0.038746167,0.08054956,-0.0136895515,-0.00716641,-0.054982424,0.059035085,0.024253605,-0.072041325,-0.004714409,0.042136513,0.002883095,-0.023395186,0.039780315,0.096730724,-0.038262647,0.03