387	4	82	On another hand, the worker’s interactions can be classified indirectly from the robot\nsensor data, and the operational context can be classified from the interaction duration, as\nwell as if the interaction was soft or hard, with what part of the robot it took place (tool or\nlink), and if it was a planned interaction or accidental. To achieve the soft object/hard object\ninteraction classification from robot torque measurements, ref. [ 92] employed a widely\nused neural network, the ResNet, achieving 98% accuracy on the test dataset.	3. Results	87	2	\N	\N	{}	[-0.084376395,-0.07513178,-0.01816616,0.031082205,0.04913117,-0.027789706,0.06685581,0.018651586,-0.050792407,0.0054685497,-0.03594912,0.020368626,-0.023874229,0.01504496,-0.08800712,-0.014943685,0.14246015,0.045000535,-0.038207866,0.07796421,0.033351023,0.0139425155,0.049667366,-0.011435346,-0.030415945,0.032055333,0.045591097,0.02153829,0.015411968,-0.030370018,-0.005978706,0.015828367,-0.02581366,0.041918263,-0.06520894,0.08854917,0.048536714,0.0072073485,-0.010723385,-0.036705747,-0.02234971,-0.009751974,0.1056905,-0.05077566,0.11527685,0.11731345,0.003433329,-0.021250144,-0.01881364,0.05591905,-0.08381178,0.02140098,0.058814812,0.014635613,-0.010598773,0.03871149,0.013680886,0.0086647775,0.02530313,0.05613227,0.086815536,-0.04241549,0.07641368,0.021818303,0.008549201,0.048484664,-0.03200886,-0.114553645,-0.0146067,-0.08821949,0.05451557,0.0039607193,-0.046636324,-0.015037924,0.020834204,-0.07510353,-0.00043743904,-0.025544956,0.018049018,-0.036715403,-0.0023526356,-0.03110743,0.013746615,-0.013574877,0.018230224,0.04590221,-0.0023813013,0.0615713,-0.07559786,-0.016494423,0.033202294,-0.0467486,-0.08084806,-0.051939618,0.002504696,-0.012482901,0.01685538,0.038151514,-0.058790546,0.020415958,-0.044778712,-0.03536885,-0.053829923,-0.0039108726,-0.03883417,0.039656013,-0.0024395424,-0.091126256,0.009208657,-0.01807633,-0.051592648,-0.07599691,-0.05993659,-0.057353664,-0.008620558,-0.08070024,-0.0509