358	4	53	Typically, the focus of the papers is on the\ntechnological implementation, using the tasks as a way to evaluate the proposed solution,\ninstead of validating it in the expected operational context, environment, and user type.\n3.1.3. Design Optimization\nSeveral requirements and their trade-offs need to be considered when determining\nthe best design parameters for a particular application or task, i.e., design optimization. This can be challenging when the design space is large and high-dimensional, requiring\nthe use of efficient algorithms to explore and evaluate a representative subset of designs.	3. Results	89	3	\N	\N	{}	[-0.07503457,0.09637096,0.0022331597,-0.0753886,-0.0040902235,-0.08947835,-0.012877436,0.055274386,-0.068845555,0.012902874,-0.15345018,0.018422201,0.03520585,0.0034668979,-0.04587927,-0.007226266,0.11541353,-0.048953697,0.03859223,0.0052782916,0.0887333,-0.018309757,0.04128724,-0.050172105,-0.053807843,0.012863323,-0.008668494,-0.058556866,0.025244063,0.007918736,0.07801242,0.07877854,0.025143027,-0.02933882,-0.003334424,0.065614454,-0.05895146,-0.020265484,0.0146822,0.025127763,-0.110232875,-0.010251108,0.015047488,0.0314247,0.05142221,-0.03512074,-0.075862415,-0.05487215,-0.109262235,-0.011010307,-0.05302642,-0.02077207,-0.01272485,-0.05146711,0.037177287,-0.03069089,0.027551286,-0.022887122,0.015942693,-0.012155614,0.044055335,-0.034971904,-0.081334636,-0.008618414,0.06111903,0.038432192,0.008626856,-0.09500019,-0.021474088,0.0077314437,-0.03888239,0.07607949,-0.014378048,-0.03555784,0.006567744,-0.010632185,-0.007476592,-0.0011552422,-0.026709227,-0.1138596,0.079998255,0.0027696816,-0.061185695,0.035227787,0.10195147,0.009101241,-0.12294506,-0.030722247,0.10389465,0.0201409,0.05885384,-0.054380674,-0.08812926,-0.013889297,-0.0043001263,-0.04471714,0.008455794,-0.0459032,0.007032245,0.052118544,-0.010321462,0.008172903,0.07023499,-0.027349863,0.032757867,-0.006352811,-0.008810678,0.03315654,-0.024969274,-0.031647652,0.029484117,-0