390	4	85	Reaching good robustness and generalization to new human subjects is a\ncommon issue with systems that aim to model human behavior. The work of [ 85] was\nable to capture the driver’s preferences and variability with a Hierarchical Reinforcement\nLearning model, for an adaptive and fairness-aware personalized ADAS. The method in-\nvolves using three interacting RL agents to learn to adapt to intra-, inter-and multi-human\nstate variability, applying Q-learning-based algorithms.	3. Results	70	3	\N	\N	{}	[-0.06379244,-0.06935118,0.016150044,0.06445799,-0.01802908,0.027710218,0.067210294,0.005051414,-0.020526476,-0.005777456,-0.06790877,-0.06829317,0.035481878,0.08087586,-0.002471402,0.012645032,0.13562803,0.02759157,-0.050668303,-0.00447186,0.052003995,0.04014679,-0.007846045,0.008154955,-0.034811698,8.538471e-05,0.019222163,-0.018343983,0.032634694,-0.026932567,0.09073328,-0.039672744,0.12861253,-0.09814484,-0.084768005,-0.023342658,-0.08317317,-0.027919747,-0.027246403,0.008948231,-0.07641185,0.00047358643,-0.050390344,-0.0072531654,0.07841798,0.036547158,0.026393373,-0.0407815,0.025006218,-0.070830986,0.015961593,0.016279077,0.058265846,0.02854508,0.0064890436,0.027799172,-0.010736376,0.07983623,-0.022822779,-0.019716647,-0.020038659,-0.13414234,-0.01626492,0.043094434,-0.03804485,0.050828498,-0.06214288,0.014177777,-0.0077107972,-0.061259434,-0.050714552,0.03421939,-0.030742124,-0.015168783,0.09799294,-0.032698885,-0.0009951344,-0.041565247,0.07535918,-0.016452918,0.012660818,-0.010756919,-0.064625114,0.019009536,0.14665902,-0.010858418,-0.018811813,0.073462635,-0.017501244,-0.016467152,-0.048602942,0.0049039656,0.024836693,-0.031027164,-0.07401703,0.036148712,0.025759673,-0.047964923,0.028037282,0.09345157,0.019216284,-0.005731975,-0.09540251,0.07004417,0.033388436,0.011519321,0.0017288072,0.005769233,0.014501372,-0.064895265,0.011828882,-0.019374417,0.014415895,0.050733816,-0.002116975,0.037591536,0.029951775,0.053201202,0.029576529,0.036830824,-0.03658