402	4	97	A multi-modal physiological approach was also adopted by [ 99,102]. Ref. [ 99] em-\nployed EEG, eye activity, and heart rate variability (HRV) to assess the mental workload\neffects of changing task load in tracking and collision prediction tasks. With a dataset of\n24 participants using multiple regression, 54.3% of the variance in the tracking task perfor-\nmance values could be explained by the model. For the collision prediction task, 61.7% of\nthe variance in the results was explained by the model.	3. Results	82	4	\N	\N	{}	[0.06278855,-0.04684833,0.035647064,0.006024637,0.08009379,-0.028668769,0.0961916,0.011569448,0.032200456,-0.0061393282,-0.0046181283,-0.05322321,-0.010189604,0.046177655,0.0039638276,-0.05000603,0.052362118,-0.00659944,-0.057465326,0.03791333,0.09211109,0.013286689,-0.014554779,-0.0025138666,-0.04049125,0.09028125,-0.060777605,-0.0012283477,-0.042473022,-0.055560462,0.044828884,-0.08252882,0.04283724,0.015825221,-0.1069339,-0.025831642,-0.005483779,-0.00081777805,-0.037265845,0.001597739,-0.12568203,-0.03792574,-0.008466073,0.020052547,0.08181106,0.056770217,-0.004632271,-0.09251552,-0.03931914,-0.02573171,-0.024075372,-0.08223893,0.12654859,0.0020642166,0.053996295,-0.035135396,0.027273426,0.00082107435,-0.011691115,-0.037685852,-0.10154787,-0.0032512133,0.03573968,-0.034190755,0.06272686,0.041322585,0.019332975,-0.050772183,-0.042822607,-0.027789474,-0.005851013,-0.039814856,-0.03916022,-0.10225892,0.039802797,0.048064195,-0.06827032,-0.046036623,0.04762855,-0.029457755,-0.0050003473,-0.061513938,-0.04433965,-0.010833949,0.08319753,-0.0142598655,0.015910998,0.07123692,-0.0024007086,0.024851572,-0.039677363,-0.059694234,0.014263035,0.026662523,-0.036658313,0.062155962,-0.11068723,0.034299493,0.04304458,-0.028014092,-0.0066460273,0.014656105,-0.004456165,0.11486942,-0.016106647,0.020842377,0.080299586,0.0003198764,-0.015700031,0.025866004,-0.027287262,0.040046304,-0.0103534395,0.054882642,0.034815315,0.01752175,-0.056391712,0.125043