418	4	113	Alternatively, ref. [ 115] proposed visualizations to assist engineers of railway signaling\nsystems in model checking, by aiding in invariant mining. Reinforcement learning was\nemployed in a first step, through simulation, to maximize the unique state observations\nof a Markov Decision Process and generate a dataset for invariant mining. The proposed\nvisualizations aimed to increase the readability of the suggested invariants, which can be\nused to constrain the model checking to those states that are reachable.	3. Results	76	3	\N	\N	{}	[-0.034877785,-0.040836286,-0.042690475,0.023922682,0.07456818,0.018955186,0.043382775,-0.02223025,-0.05606771,0.03856069,-0.054962933,-0.0044989833,0.029093316,0.060680654,-0.09429201,0.06054916,0.024203517,-0.031376965,-0.012846647,-0.1319926,-0.010506542,-0.10369027,-0.05322058,0.018022466,-0.04174771,0.02727515,0.063647404,0.03588672,-0.019880822,-0.044048067,-0.11246392,-0.06643448,0.048186205,-0.0897021,-0.020940337,0.0025657092,0.04088637,-0.03214907,0.014910151,0.009824394,-0.06402549,-0.03792345,0.010278067,0.04263005,0.049896225,0.03835066,0.00184469,-0.09906789,-0.034034226,-0.06934746,-0.015202238,-0.03120295,0.03947724,-0.008696722,0.0068010497,0.008853092,0.012611027,0.0017986523,-0.010759493,-0.01240933,-0.021702608,-0.020487642,4.1949894e-05,-0.012362637,-0.002731381,0.061252475,-0.07672285,0.102507524,0.067443736,-0.017266707,-0.032464318,0.017673442,-0.013430026,-0.045084544,-0.006153619,0.042821504,-0.050768245,0.0015827668,0.012256088,-0.12891711,-0.15115952,-0.02942296,-0.028357016,0.011594854,0.028123602,-0.016719328,-0.018909644,0.0038076935,0.12427595,-0.009987461,0.021789232,0.090177126,0.047043797,0.030233461,-0.0047190743,0.096640415,-0.012452809,0.0033617644,-0.0033559268,0.083010875,-0.007337248,0.06273759,0.07210772,0.015397257,0.036098193,-0.0098152645,0.008833425,0.024532257,0.07789904,-0.10254607,0.05075033,-0.0077931616,0.05348328,0.092133574,-0.029256124,0.016164284,-0.056622803,-0.0196