477	4	172	An aspect of collaborative intelligence that was missed in the reviewed works is the\nfact that in many cyber–physical systems, the intelligent machine might have to interact\nwith many humans in different contexts, and the humans might interact with different\nsystem instantiations, sharing the same knowledge base [ 2]. Computational techniques\nsuch as federated learning (also referred as collaborative learning) need to come into play\nto achieve this multi-human multi-agent collaboration scenario. We provide a summary of recommended actions (Figure 7) taken from the analysis of\nthe literature on the safe application of AI to collaborative intelligence problems.	4. Discussion	98	3	\N	\N	{}	[0.012181594,-0.028283533,-0.04884769,-0.013331159,0.0003934585,0.011604266,0.017916877,-0.01441706,-0.038857285,0.027756251,-0.015278932,-0.006201375,0.06322613,0.029503277,-0.007857538,-0.0010860533,0.010032596,-0.07618031,-0.045441482,-0.0646646,-0.024547447,0.0029507154,-0.0008784607,-0.015456171,-0.069525905,0.0038991359,0.048480015,-0.08933971,-0.048874535,-0.0009498413,0.017282937,-0.007979592,0.022045325,-0.0112039,-0.04526578,0.06553044,-0.0162532,0.07868733,0.04298558,-0.009192594,-0.070915565,-0.051316466,-0.03563512,-0.016458655,0.020307433,0.06803614,-0.082145594,-0.030677805,0.01936585,0.011024565,-0.115302,-0.040093306,0.042120457,0.08614943,0.055756763,0.0071194097,-0.03415932,-0.045376536,-0.048923448,-0.06383551,-0.00078598846,-0.06415351,0.043413203,0.023241263,0.025780644,0.03354019,-0.02222106,0.020518195,-0.009035952,-0.054641727,-0.013661251,0.034754783,-0.013345493,-0.060540393,-0.008476868,0.04598332,-0.08184935,-0.093100555,0.05037334,-0.062682725,-0.020515027,0.07926958,-0.022725146,0.01951816,0.036099944,0.0033261075,-0.027836217,0.017175036,0.0015700025,-0.012076925,-0.0070740865,0.033187777,0.057146274,0.017700478,0.007387482,0.014950345,-0.007383865,-0.03866577,-0.0316082,0.057791177,-0.05527782,0.05900975,-0.0037944997,0.02559445,0.0322