483	5	0	ENGAGING WITH AI: H OWINTERFACE DESIGN SHAPES\nHUMAN -AI C OLLABORATION IN HIGH-STAKES\nDECISION -MAKING\nZichen Chen\nUniversity of California, Santa Barbara\nzichen_chen@ucsb.edu∗Yunhao Luo\nUniversity of California, Santa Barbara\nyunhaoluo@ucsb.edu\nMisha Sra\nUniversity of California, Santa Barbara\nsra@ucsb.edu As reliance on AI systems for decision-making grows, it becomes critical to ensure that human\nusers can appropriately balance trust in AI suggestions with their own judgment, especially in high-\nstakes domains like healthcare. However, human + AI teams have been shown to perform worse\nthan AI alone, with evidence indicating automation bias as the reason for poorer performance, par-\nticularly because humans tend to follow AI’s recommendations even when they are incorrect.	Preamble	111	3	\N	\N	{}	[0.020879991,0.00846756,0.014777391,0.0030334105,0.026922023,-0.04307329,0.06931731,0.0892193,0.04593984,0.027235733,-0.08521367,-0.034014054,0.060107738,-0.01361055,0.03467381,-0.05815686,0.06687712,-0.07612915,-0.043506876,-0.05604648,-0.04979762,-0.029075978,0.0058125523,-0.051121414,-0.008901777,-0.061236646,-0.05666994,-0.04918182,-0.017978385,-0.05322804,0.012478016,-0.04578467,0.118177325,-0.032643583,-0.063111104,-0.014723595,-0.07515847,0.02800687,0.0012723329,-0.033638354,-0.06250661,-0.035026982,0.024343496,0.01280254,0.025634993,0.04404704,-0.02267347,-0.083254136,-0.018335814,0.03142213,-0.15247653,-0.04763691,0.079248235,-0.048936874,-0.034985624,0.06890737,0.015196312,0.0935445,0.007541979,-0.025119947,-0.0074887886,-0.049826168,0.014023986,0.011340879,0.06854206,0.06597276,0.0024312048,-0.044529356,-0.051272593,-0.0013625742,0.114694424,0.030121513,-0.008329351,-0.017837761,0.072541535,0.0457195,-0.009460158,-0.08590432,0.1256889,-0.05965455,-0.035866942,-0.009996124,-0.018567145,0.09698948,0.003836803,0.014761966,-0.0017947678,-0.071574114,0.03563439,0.0129646575,-0.006341932,-0.09070156,-0.009871614,-0.0088985115,0.048582833,0.077226