490	5	7	Users often weigh the cognitive cost (System 2) of evaluating AI suggestions against\nperceived benefits, potentially defaulting to uncritical acceptance (System 1) if the effort seems too high [41, 42, 39]. Conversely, under-trust can lead to the dismissal of valuable AI support, limiting the potential benefits of human-AI\ncollaboration. Users may rely excessively on their intuitions (System 1) or engage in overly critical analysis (System\n2) that can both discount AI contributions. Strategies to promote more analytical thinking and mitigate cognitive biases\ninherent in System 1 thinking have recently been explored [27].	AIAI	92	4	\N	\N	{}	[0.0017244266,-0.011215294,-0.017919945,-0.015402663,0.07588611,-0.03179101,0.113633186,0.120064095,0.058008384,0.019379297,-0.069549546,-0.03974346,0.057308313,-0.008479014,0.028681813,-0.013997875,0.060790762,-0.0685297,-0.0284726,-0.05852477,-0.052070957,-0.046313617,-0.04021859,-0.05483659,-0.013414027,-0.04931489,-0.064595446,-0.03911914,-0.019079832,0.007557737,0.04399051,-0.0019151636,0.034839153,0.0046978616,-0.04780073,-0.047975335,-0.061636668,0.077627145,0.028266536,-0.024652326,-0.06585155,0.022433322,0.03513915,-0.0068813884,0.013725552,-0.009403436,-0.029913101,-0.0045137713,0.03275844,-0.011326737,-0.13027036,-0.0028262225,0.011750868,-0.025982646,-0.019715691,0.03565771,0.0073500364,0.08280279,-0.070693895,-0.011383715,-0.031028692,-0.078331366,0.029396191,-0.0151021,0.06521661,0.041919574,-0.011730058,9.0017646e-05,-0.10106985,0.037291028,0.057676405,0.06079932,-0.011380144,-0.08735439,0.038692083,0.029349593,-0.033466745,-0.044423185,0.07142661,-0.06646503,-0.009732106,0.05361327,-0.007677598,0.06804506,-0.007380402,-0.007398455,0.016099012,-0.04654499,0.066457376,0.008430034,0.059828524,-0.08794247,-0.00060518365,0.00037539224,0.06988198,0.096504405,-0.046472482,0.027704325,-0.12822996,0.050830737,-0.0043817433,0.036474492,0.034267243,-0.05896158,-0.003363506,-0.013537235,0.086323775,-0.01612612,0.05