495	5	12	The contribution of our work is threefold. First, we provide empirical evidence on the effectiveness of different\ndecision support mechanisms in influencing user trust, engagement, and decision-making. Second, we contribute to\nunderstanding of trust dynamics in human-AI interaction by exploring how different explanation types and CFFs influ-\nence trust calibration. And lastly, we present a methodological approach for evaluating decision support mechanisms\nthrough controlled experiments, isolating the effects of individual explanation and CFF types. Our approach can be\nadapted to other domains beyond healthcare.	AIAI	84	5	\N	\N	{}	[-0.031224547,-0.09854546,-0.00048195448,0.013769688,0.1086635,-0.023955029,0.11565804,0.047781345,0.026694432,0.01941349,-0.030213347,-0.08055659,0.025257632,0.030230155,0.0020502869,-0.056223907,0.02595557,-0.05670053,-0.120460354,0.026303992,-0.0027192156,-0.06009232,0.002180573,-0.0142106,-0.041097213,-0.05722475,-0.040679507,-0.033173747,-0.040512677,0.004427322,0.055331275,0.025745539,0.028791308,-0.029513812,-0.082364805,-0.02003515,-0.034410276,0.02540786,-0.061748933,-0.048407327,-0.087729424,-0.034218825,0.092748694,0.04288287,0.07273268,0.04704071,0.00014668849,-0.0095307315,-0.012518593,0.040150147,-0.1280085,0.014361351,-0.016880842,-0.0030044487,-0.035716176,0.0009978074,0.023340434,0.057476304,-0.03810278,-0.014375839,0.0038856275,-0.042281426,-0.001706753,0.028797567,0.041979637,0.11688893,-0.045293506,-0.0615028,-0.020048449,-0.075311646,0.02351654,0.060093887,0.015706668,-0.052818216,-0.013389639,0.029503245,-0.019195614,0.0043455176,0.07364022,-0.037082028,0.016938843,0.05998235,0.02944004,0.039308663,0.012739825,-0.04075715,0.061768588,-0.05654278,0.030905038,0.06387988,0.030245889,-0.05492126,-0.028528783,0.017082812,-0.03493363,0.054719295,-0.09149499,-0.029744215,-0.059793636,-0.001463147,-0.069626324,0.0042000064,-0.009783833,-0.04964952,0.045871112,0.031812176,0.05425967,-0.030274283,0.06714066,0.01703