586	5	103	Our findings support the hypothesis that balanced EIL is crucial for optimizing human-AI collaboration (H3) , es-\npecially in high-stakes environments like diabetes management. Conditions involving textual explanations (C1) and\nAI CLs (C3) show significant improvements in user accuracy and decision-making, as these mechanisms provide\ntransparency and help users engage critically with AI outputs without overwhelming them. Previous research has\nsimilarly demonstrated that well-calibrated transparency and interpretability can build more effective reliance cali-\nbration, allowing users to rely on AI outputs more appropriately without falling into over-reliance or under-reliance\ntraps [85, 90, 28, 91, 46].	3.3.1 Cognitive Load Management	95	3	\N	\N	{}	[-0.015866218,0.0033559764,-0.02307668,0.025598364,0.073075324,0.0028200692,0.06743633,0.030039618,0.047959056,0.012242613,-0.084120624,-0.042090535,-0.020753467,-0.02825601,0.02266852,-0.065663256,0.049694493,-0.043002322,-0.057577044,-0.065512225,0.05123027,0.031752545,0.024594286,0.034872085,-0.0123698,0.011472612,-0.030269034,-0.07427845,0.022754496,-0.0027058949,-0.013382997,-0.05144351,0.10280042,0.008453476,-0.17628287,0.07123548,-0.032620743,-0.026208721,-0.063661635,-0.074161574,-0.05404338,-0.015845696,-0.013592068,0.020783111,0.039786,-0.0071238438,-0.084683724,-0.050895434,0.048887663,0.06036591,-0.10583657,-0.016973786,0.07176765,-0.032670625,-0.017928075,0.051017445,-0.01733697,0.05828562,-0.04055358,-0.06490899,-0.033534043,-0.07154092,0.04085347,0.09055913,0.12969525,0.019821689,0.017991181,0.0024345452,-0.097042896,-0.022393752,-0.01314652,0.07997713,-0.007688933,0.001521384,0.03881173,0.09520371,-0.027948463,-0.033363797,0.048624758,0.029733855,-0.0039839074,-0.0064744465,0.051155616,0.062546894,-0.020034563,-0.018527688,0.048911016,-0.037940897,-0.008012474,0.011276505,0.00787873,-0.030819321,0.011644992,0.02737334,-0.0021916241,0.08468767,-0.04077878,-0.045383148,-0.07711731,0.050914045,-