617	5	134	We employ statistical methods, adapted to different comparisons, to evaluate the impact of AI explanation mechanisms. These analyses are designed to test our hypotheses regarding user behavior and performance under different conditions.\n1. Reliance on AI Suggestions (H1): To investigate user reliance on AI suggestions, we apply the McNemar\ntest [106]. This test is appropriate for paired nominal data, enabling us to evaluate whether the proportion\nof users aligning with AI suggestions differed significantly when the AI’s suggestions are correct versus\nEngaging with AI\nincorrect. The McNemar test provides insights into the degree of over- (or under-) reliance by analyzing\nchanges in user behavior based on the accuracy of the AI’s outputs.\n2.	6.5 Statistical Analysis	113	5	\N	\N	{}	[-0.027213218,-0.10813784,0.0669279,0.030339114,0.068489306,-0.0076893885,0.07385002,0.1248691,0.024130402,0.0055635544,-0.05907811,-0.05600291,-0.0025678321,-0.024470063,0.040768623,0.007679591,0.10910315,-0.030699706,-0.017470194,-0.055210836,0.048268605,-0.013250985,0.016533745,-0.03859808,-0.034485843,0.025040831,-0.02867131,-0.016894467,-0.016300835,0.040067505,-0.023521736,0.040449955,-0.0009731868,0.027403584,-0.12960437,-0.025852464,-0.08594088,0.11994894,0.011246078,-0.039889675,-0.1448975,-0.02212697,0.09092378,0.003618208,0.041819327,0.041528653,-0.054748476,0.030300247,-0.046382114,0.09898997,-0.1449587,0.049473263,0.064435296,-0.05233228,-0.0050999364,0.010825867,0.050125677,0.10292028,0.055723213,-0.044169363,0.00048233205,-0.04174494,-0.023819331,0.008200221,0.043542013,0.044160154,-0.041586958,-0.050119996,-0.072921515,0.027512692,0.06394499,0.058124,-0.075337306,-0.02332696,0.019674867,0.050037663,-0.016958024,0.026395854,0.06558467,-0.03399144,-0.07287295,0.014843982,0.018170035,0.016419735,0.036706656,-0.019814655,0.062885664,-0.008117828,0.014048721,0.030360693,0.08483654,-0.030179072,-0.019811975,-0.012432633,0.016398024,0.11354239,-0.08214844,-0.0470596