712	6	55	Frequency of the papers in each publication year. The time distribution of the publications highlights distinct phases of HAIC develop-\nment: Early Research (2018–2020): This stage primarily focused on theoretical frameworks\nand conceptual definitions, with limited empirical studies. Development Phase ( 2021–2023 ):\nInformatics 2025 ,12, 135 12 of 36\nThis stage involved diversified research methods, expanded application domains, and ex-\ntensive experimental validation. Recent Trends (2024–2025): This stage focused on (1) the\nincreased application of generative AI in collaborative settings, (2) greater emphasis on\ninteraction models and adaptive system design, (3) deeper explorations of ethical con-\nsiderations and trust mechanisms, and (4) expansion into diverse professional fields and\nreal-world applications. Research Domains’ Distribution\nThe literature reveals four distinct research clusters that capture the evolving land-\nscape of HAIC, with Decision Support and Augmentation (35 papers, 42.7%) leads, focusing\non enhancing decision making in fields like medicine and marketing.	3. Results	149	5	\N	\N	{}	[-0.07386062,-0.04251526,-0.024525208,-0.010948881,0.02514204,0.013289808,-0.0061300257,0.03664523,0.05978251,0.05848264,-0.0740939,0.02057945,0.043658495,0.02448441,-0.0019267763,0.0065332786,-0.034064643,-0.085673116,-0.067253,0.014388869,-0.0981827,0.061053608,0.0526296,-0.0070227906,-0.055538755,-0.0023702013,0.033281457,-0.08155604,-0.04895375,-0.021865709,0.079211906,0.145462,0.027142448,-0.010571207,-0.08400645,0.13673036,-0.010030921,0.03693274,0.052747518,-0.0016441172,-0.034609243,-0.08925647,-0.03048155,-0.04113921,0.0488661,-0.03841352,0.0039374293,0.0059010596,-0.03900304,0.004165147,-0.109086424,-0.047228947,0.0241264,0.040412974,-0.008038461,0.006685575,0.029717047,0.05399466,-0.061045773,-0.038053077,-0.030027095,-0.012943012,-0.03473636,0.007304018,0.04050161,0.066819675,-0.066238314,0.08378233,-0.03317858,-0.108264826,0.081992