723	6	66	The divergence between these positions reflects a deeper theoretical uncertainty about\nhuman metacognitive capacity in HAIC. The Bayesian integration view assumes humans\ncan accurately weight AI recommendations against their own intuitions, but the per-\nformance paradox evidence suggests this assumption is frequently violated. If humans\nsystematically mis-calibrate their reliance, over-relying when AI errs and under-relying\nwhen AI excels, then complementarity’s benefits may be inherently limited regardless of\nrole architecture design. The emotional intelligence preservation perspective sidesteps this\nproblem by restricting complementarity to domains where AI contributions are auxiliary\nrather than central, but this retreat substantially narrows the scope of effective human–AI\ncollaboration.	3. Results	102	4	\N	\N	{}	[0.038645398,-0.07654243,0.038744517,0.022316562,0.024802221,0.03758924,0.022667788,-0.006586896,0.049329415,-0.008296813,-0.08120863,-0.011950345,0.002092056,-0.041719094,0.011672071,0.0810841,0.019217879,-0.02034381,-0.07786366,8.9617155e-05,-0.03253646,0.023235396,-0.013192785,-0.06394183,-0.0067050327,0.04364688,-0.013169775,-0.04173717,0.020105613,-0.0052896705,0.06434936,-0.0012988697,0.030677572,-0.004627546,-0.03326374,0.06989005,-0.017860495,0.01700018,0.025643535,-0.077802904,-0.07481315,0.003747299,-0.033037182,-0.024379186,0.032416765,0.03188242,-0.048109908,-0.09208441,-0.011943626,-0.010338455,-0.10821229,0.009574845,-0.03626738,0.066783145,0.0036487533,0.11341548,0.02738873,-0.021297615,-0.060728125,-0.019600855,-0.078622036,-0.020334957,0.00953707,-0.018284643,0.10283213,0.027339045,-0.055082604,0.0010112,-0.02498694,0.008354428,0.0553408,0.022674467,-0.031043941,-0.025344897,0.061672576,0.08727256,-0.005234012,-0.07124224,0.09133021,-0.08893262,-0.008541531,0.051612884,0.0033227506,0.055146333,0.03425906,-0.029014453,0.015648253,-0.05663688,0.008588785,0.08301061,0.06353924,-0.076108694,0.03961244,-0.04169696,0.0581421