732	6	75	The field’s reliance on small\nsamples of technology-familiar academics (Zheng et al. with eight pharmacists [ 75]; Park\nwith twenty participants [ 76]; and Meske and Ünal with twenty-four participants [ 72])\nraises serious questions about whether findings would replicate with technology-naive pop-\nulations or in domains where users lack the baseline expertise to evaluate AI capabilities. Until research addresses these foundational uncertainties—through studies with diverse\npopulations, realistic AI systems with known imperfections, and longitudinal tracking of\nadaptation effects—recommendations for adaptive design remain premature.\n3.2.3.	3. Results	85	2	\N	\N	{}	[-0.01589516,-0.004464966,0.013003819,0.03358172,0.056621525,-0.044307895,0.0016848852,0.09019123,-0.0073346416,-0.05417198,-0.10522912,0.008533366,0.029163213,-0.040085293,-0.024490198,-0.017399607,0.057656206,-0.057863485,-0.0002404823,-0.026218662,-0.07593723,0.012037914,0.1357746,-0.020030897,-0.017045904,0.043662842,-0.016380968,-0.034154635,-0.005458991,-0.010875247,0.04470695,0.07982268,-0.0073143747,-0.041651126,-0.032150015,0.004514003,-0.029053723,0.13258672,0.09341515,-0.009083264,-0.037664056,-0.06439031,0.005857839,0.0079250755,0.070270665,-0.04560245,-0.061209552,-0.01660387,-0.024843393,0.051273406,-0.10481254,-0.09870016,0.031051738,-0.07622444,-0.050106343,0.029662458,0.008839353,0.06533753,0.012807959,0.035162743,0.016908498,-0.043238178,0.029381456,0.053538762,0.054797072,0.078483224,-0.025167946,0.0018196179,-0.007177996,-0.041803278,-0.012196505,0.07774752,-0.05401391,0.06682999,0.05840901,-0.027848175,-0.007879846,0.015447119,0.042397268,0.0142839225,0.015170366,-0.009168213,-0.09926766,0.071999595,0.017346911,-0.023294736,-0.015783697,-0.016844923,0.04205117,-0.028787319,0.0811993,-0.0200382,-0.017921766,-0.020640844,0.029426878,0.0016060584,0.0054599685,-0.04164631,-0.04895658,0.03488707,-0.00085458753,0.046507467,0.032607473,0.015719514,-0.03291006,-0.016775778,0.047