740	6	83	The finding from\nLin et al. [ 81] that GPT-3 underperformed human assistants in strategic planning—despite\nbeing allocated precisely the kind of reasoning-intensive task that taxonomies would\nsuggest favoring AI—indicates that current models of AI capability may systematically\noverestimate performance in complex real-world conditions. Until allocation strategies are\nvalidated in authentic operational settings with consequential outcomes, their practical\nutility remains speculative.\n3.2.4. Strategy 4: Autonomous Reliance Calibration\nAutonomous reliance calibration shifts focus from system-level optimization to em-\npowering users to calibrate their own reliance on AI.	3. Results	86	3	\N	\N	{}	[-0.051775604,-0.050599165,-0.020690199,0.0063594,0.007866779,-0.06617929,0.04204765,-0.0012308495,-0.0071852184,0.04996151,-0.079291925,0.010318387,0.008528768,0.054259486,0.012684405,-0.04661817,0.098235786,-0.020394538,-0.020015778,-0.040534504,0.030764189,0.003305159,0.04248577,-0.031349465,0.029964173,-0.0061790035,-0.005404625,-0.12533756,-0.020936726,0.03215297,0.010224552,-0.05766366,0.07033124,-0.048865996,-0.04162045,0.07361337,-0.071135715,-0.014149895,0.085480176,0.02984529,-0.06146957,-0.022868056,-0.03505332,-0.014205,0.05963491,0.0070515033,-0.040266205,-0.039663598,-0.022361485,-0.050529677,-0.11196486,0.016456472,0.02098653,-0.08425359,-0.030944003,0.069522515,0.045943998,0.057090852,0.07063362,0.0062786187,-0.0016814045,-0.09147922,-0.012964501,-0.05411483,0.034668304,0.029996594,-0.010658862,-0.02123533,-0.06547039,-0.0040322216,0.04203822,0.09658001,-0.08603508,-0.04676882,0.06925438,0.024940176,0.008887716,-0.019123292,0.09430264,-0.06382716,0.029871328,0.04090152,-0.0153541835,0.08983128,-0.0061589535,-0.004717665,-0.020724202,-0.0059693684,0.08940722,0.033375956,0.024101969,-0.021882337,0.063988626,0.025225593,0.03554629,0.050522782,-0.034424983,-0.109727845,-0.10890769,-0.009864945,0.00717347,0.08444784,-0.060225233,-0.031004114,-0.035213