773	6	116	The paradox—simpler explanations outperforming\nsophisticated alternatives—challenges the core assumption driving XAI development that\nmore comprehensive explanations enable better decisions. Yet even this apparently ro-\nbust finding may be an artifact of the laboratory contexts in which it was established:\nVasconcelos et al.’s [ 102] ‘perfect’ explanations bear little resemblance to the imperfect\nexplanations real XAI systems produce, and Morrison et al.’s [ 104] demonstration that\nimperfect example-based explanations are more deceptive than their alternatives suggests\nthat findings from idealized conditions may reverse in deployment.	3. Results	84	2	\N	\N	{}	[-0.055042677,-0.007870222,0.03996193,0.03215554,0.17911884,-0.08801912,-0.023453316,0.08240468,-0.0055271285,0.004969995,0.0075343912,-0.04847205,0.031053346,0.014563467,0.019828469,-0.080323756,0.06649007,-0.062943675,-0.028018456,0.0003047764,-0.0076948027,-0.060205918,0.030774916,0.040401433,0.0026301497,0.03780008,-0.045184795,-0.04001952,0.0391209,-0.012149779,-0.05395576,0.079431646,0.046352174,-0.029898277,-0.021265035,0.035812616,-0.05955447,0.058079414,-0.028438324,-0.031043904,-0.06471179,-0.05162014,0.0013620616,0.014774441,-0.0073372987,-0.06768002,0.004315702,-0.035401016,-0.04283791,-0.014045768,-0.10905421,-0.029495602,-0.03556577,-0.06946183,-0.0033300214,0.00084294664,-0.029375274,0.06852692,-0.03773291,0.0071683764,0.0067098327,-0.039619334,-0.038213145,0.03450023,0.08714919,0.03795743,-0.03555625,0.005081356,-0.003169127,0.032967586,0.060701683,0.024481365,-0.0252537,-0.031782996,0.016566154,0.108987205,0.052939255,0.091730244,-0.006012489,-0.014010837,-0.0144461915,-0.072603114,-0.059238933,0.054389242,0.023503797,-0.038067922,0.029066233,-0.0833307,0.055284925,0.057653148,0.04560555,-0.0931537,0.03659868,-0.0034544459,0.11900389,0.026701579,0.053586297,-0.0023828396,-0.07025059,0.041356254,-0.0022302703,0.023916498,0.026759738,-0.08215397,0.016136665,-0.10202884,0.00286545