802	6	145	The\nunique characteristics of military decision making—including time pressure, incomplete\ninformation, and life-or-death consequences—create distinct requirements for trust calibra-\ntion and skill preservation. New frameworks emphasizing human agency, oversight, transparency, and account-\nability are being developed specifically to address the shortcomings of traditional ap-\nproaches in military contexts. However, these frameworks must balance operational\neffectiveness with ethical requirements and international humanitarian law compliance.	3. Results	63	3	\N	\N	{}	[-0.063617624,-0.0064938883,-0.07931636,-0.0824498,-0.04820391,-0.009510296,0.041599218,-0.035115562,0.05386009,0.119986765,0.040952772,0.024911404,0.04349243,0.05112881,0.0041594366,-0.016317142,-0.015557383,-0.009023323,-0.06014057,-0.00285247,0.026813613,-0.031322103,0.07487585,0.04974888,-0.06202692,-0.039318413,-0.015500499,-0.015984232,-0.06945304,-0.02295537,0.057553153,-0.01762849,0.093394995,-0.024764169,0.017588897,0.10269297,0.036568165,-0.024976386,-0.019238492,-0.006594613,-0.037346624,-0.09199837,0.053945027,0.04399151,-0.04273765,0.009560072,0.06222286,-0.0011402545,-0.047812957,0.017128874,-0.035356607,-0.043261196,-0.023470629,-0.044433467,0.020343928,-0.026172405,0.032432497,0.06336164,-0.04749436,-0.038955398,-0.06618787,0.05318589,-0.030168295,0.04492387,0.0033119195,0.08724608,0.013892084,-0.06646461,-0.012065434,-0.019555181,0.026078094,0.014034427,-0.028694808,-0.023828084,-0.06724629,0.022116695,0.041876357,0.06062577,0.09379923,-0.061614063,0.08546716,-0.00423974,-0.028052505,0.03324906,0.008749416,-0.049234282,0.074675985,-0.037067283,0.1258542,0.037128747,0.06226618,-0.08329228,0.09755826,0.010730992,0.012928276,0.035620563,0.02457275,0.03408672,-0.12463857,-0.025754105,-0.022949673,-0.07368485,-0.12537105,-0.004861218,0.041310858,0.020021435,0.028525358,-0.059350047,-0.0085086245,0.0015167119,-0.024254559,0.046987407,-0.059605446,-0.00067772565,0.068761446,0.07