816	6	159	Transparency effects present another conflict area. Some studies demonstrate that\ntransparency mechanisms improve trust calibration, while other research found that ex-\nplainable AI led to dangerous over-reliance in healthcare contexts [ 76,87,105]. This contra-\ndiction suggests context-dependent transparency effects requiring domain-specific analysis. Interactive control mechanisms show similar conflicting patterns. Several studies\ndemonstrated that user control improved outcomes, yet other research found that interac-\ntive methods may increase over-trust through co-creation effects [ 66,67,86].	3. Results	73	5	\N	\N	{}	[-0.04411565,-0.045006707,-0.029348193,-0.011615278,0.04295457,-0.008012912,0.05184307,0.019475443,0.059882276,-0.0068154596,0.01622263,0.007493012,0.07973176,-0.057972528,0.020269409,-0.048091576,0.069438286,-0.022393422,-0.111025184,-0.024524737,0.0045981198,-0.034192253,-0.010804729,0.012667246,-0.05097874,-0.0567577,-0.015360072,-0.094585605,0.025112698,0.002314115,0.08141019,-0.078336574,0.01633288,-0.046968512,-0.11212498,-0.04886447,-0.015699606,0.03783779,-0.012146758,-0.039527606,-0.045003474,-0.01658061,0.020281704,0.019503796,0.050946936,0.033416934,0.017541356,-0.010919482,-0.045394383,0.00019193775,-0.10585742,-0.041104052,0.045244716,0.011606856,-0.05597154,-0.04634184,0.02303242,0.06882869,-0.09124418,0.05078652,-0.05334374,-0.022673052,-0.012802799,0.06809989,0.059806313,0.12384553,-0.027749537,-0.005812361,-0.050096445,-0.05950424,0.06833033,0.031883147,0.053412702,-0.018661963,-0.00932981,-0.002443031,-0.039473988,0.03439421,0.058572013,-0.052040346,0.07468504,0.037023284,0.03259741,0.05056919,-0.044743694,-0.015270691,0.039725225,-0.08506411,0.027847191,0.04602692,0.039694197,0.035139143,0.026153076,0.010548971,0.034449253,-0.015280503,-0.014770365,-0.020738836,-0.0120892525,-0.0064475024,-0.052485265,0.00875051,-0.027475528,0.003028314,0.056700878,0.062092107,0.03605616,-0.049297348,0.019093014,0.077378064,-0.07416