820	6	163	Regarding synthesis methodology, while our human–AI collaborative approach\ndemonstrated substantial efficiency gains (reducing per-paper processing time from 20 to\n35 min to under 8 min) and achieved high inter-rater reliability among human researchers\n(95.2% agreement rate), several methodological considerations warrant acknowledgment. First, the quality of AI information extraction depends on prompt design, which may\ncontain systematic biases despite iterative refinement. Second, the “AI information first, hu-\nman judgment second” design may create anchoring effects, potentially influencing human\nresearchers toward AI-suggested interpretations. Although human researchers retained\nfinal decision authority and achieved high agreement rates, we cannot entirely rule out\nsuch cognitive influences. Third, the AI models used for information extraction may reflect\nbiases present in their training datasets, particularly in how they interpret and categorize\nresearch contributions.	3. Results	126	5	\N	\N	{}	[-0.075397335,0.03142264,-0.029857378,0.039171644,0.07716473,-0.058774084,0.0074992403,0.020255547,0.054999646,-0.013769822,-0.101444855,0.046107884,0.016662411,-0.016984638,-0.013982069,0.0008966042,0.046039514,-0.03314823,-0.035115916,-0.044760264,0.026973033,0.06453358,0.010604037,-0.04679881,0.050462194,-0.0019664671,-0.03442961,-0.055279497,0.033715557,0.01459462,0.039003775,0.023493716,0.11565853,0.020178102,-0.07777121,0.04576786,-0.0630137,0.0869452,0.03644439,0.029940011,-0.04467291,-0.01862592,0.022472668,0.020827167,0.09176528,0.009005619,-0.08484484,-0.037316523,-0.060091704,0.094885945,-0.13922635,0.052531622,0.06266059,-0.007750199,-0.06028099,0.023018707,-0.017832834,0.070388846,-0.044031657,-0.045672473,-0.08771105,-0.06889201,-0.045028087,-0.019495584,0.086880445,-0.012028244,-0.01129617,-0.007003038,-0.04270729,0.0241176,0.03484518,0.09822177,-0.036178987,-0.034166656,0.0061636493,0.017220894,-0.039200995,0.043241423,0.07881036,-0.127