830	7	1	2Federal Institute for Vocational Education and Training, Robert-Schuman-Platz 3, 53175 Bonn, Germany;\nconein@bibb.de (S.C.); thomas.felkl@bibb.de (T.F.)\n*Correspondence: marina.klostermann@ruhr-uni-bochum.de; Tel.: +49-176-70833974\nAbstract: The infrequent use of skills relevant in non-routine situations in highly automated and high-\nrisk industries is a major safety issue. The infrequent use of skills can lead to skill decay. Research on\nskill decay has a long history, but not much is known about the relevant factors and refresher inter-\nventions to attenuate skill decay in highly automated environments. In the present study, a scoping\nreview was conducted to determine whether the well-known factors in skill decay research are also\nrelevant for complex cognitive skill decay and to identify refresher interventions that are deemed\neffective for attenuating decay.	44801 Bochum, Germany; annette.kluge@ruhr-uni-bochum.de	120	4	\N	\N	{}	[-0.003193156,-0.018767765,0.0058903876,0.047657974,0.026363762,0.0032743241,0.015503492,0.07758761,-0.066112064,0.0026879243,0.015820682,0.044789046,0.022558462,0.022073174,-0.017108532,-0.028152524,-0.027822444,-5.8374455e-05,-0.093979105,-0.052202027,-0.0003516132,-0.037058845,0.002384523,0.015750216,-0.014359035,-0.00465677,-0.057116926,-0.09716952,-0.014191853,0.012172197,-0.023262369,0.044851344,-0.0202073,0.00040244445,0.030320426,0.03380708,0.05256852,0.074885346,0.031178538,-0.06119482,-0.07433795,-0.07684056,-0.0044501205,-0.032575168,0.063458554,0.019370098,0.0077434233,-0.058037374,-0.031049788,0.02372483,-0.08013989,-0.023119237,0.096567035,-0.009658136,0.034247607,0.050885487,0.06711183,0.0708789,-0.05947248,0.01013209,-0.049065057,-0.058266375,-0.059781358,-0.047831822,-0.058953747,0.033453465,-0.04708792,-0.07483317,-0.014558362,0.10255175,-0.059035335,-0.063085996,-0.09458456,0.015664862,0.08153397,-0.036526,-0.042649917,-0.09315066,0.025044786,-0.08217996,0.07179903,-0.002531834,-0.021484872,-0.04148443