896	7	67	Team Skill Decay\nThe majority of skill decay literature in this scoping review dealt with individual skill\ndecay. Additionally, the concept of team skill decay emerged as a key concept when con-\nsidering non-routine situations in high-risk and highly automated environments. As with\nindividual skill decay, the retention of a task is inﬂuenced by the number of action steps\nand the number of specialized skills and cognitive demands [ 98].	3. Results	70	3	\N	\N	{}	[0.028853552,0.003160249,-0.011260093,0.030762076,0.049041968,-0.009022852,0.0032989027,0.006561878,-0.0023441557,0.008501085,-0.0050269915,0.100248456,0.01892238,0.07176526,0.0077990857,-0.061126165,-0.07816613,-0.051938865,-0.080271825,-0.04479529,-0.043200023,-0.0633474,-0.004193449,0.04739632,-0.0076420465,-0.05254124,-0.052485224,-0.08474649,-0.0035764747,-0.021606272,-0.038447354,0.057245333,0.05446811,0.001074481,-0.02602116,0.08759025,0.019148681,0.044224788,0.007105927,-0.030569792,-0.05102142,-0.028806312,-0.017516956,-0.008280795,0.02186454,0.055130184,-0.015682265,-0.03760888,-0.048488908,0.051333535,-0.065441564,-0.047536213,0.05136945,-0.001946315,0.079747945,0.01427264,0.06260645,-0.0011455952,-0.04537351,0.009000579,-0.0098044695,-0.069788806,-0.0649443,-0.027017998,-0.010092189,0.015156838,-0.0070025637,-0.047500916,-0.024972327,0.08360632,-0.0989394,-0.054322418,-0.08133431,0.0014301619,0.039160416,0.04825711,-0.009372929,-0.123171695,-0.011382529,-0.08178287,0.032915857,-0.0481703,-0.017609451,0.029336939,-0.038776465,-0.056547213,0.01377596,0.011970287,0.085079275,-0.009592166,-0.0035402083,0.039664675,0.053768244,-0.04049271,-0.024536908,0.08830415,-0.0046170754,0.055923272,-0.050142843,0.011545972,-0.047338177,-0.044901453,-0.015876856,-0.0046791346,0.005775371,0.021243976,0.044076685,0.0029103241,0.021207381,0.046091978,-0.032380454,0.015626704,-0.019504087,0.028904155,-0.0049312473,0.058066588,-0.075841345,0.055164866,-0.107007205,0.074051455,0.13919483,-0.0034317025,0.032