934	8	15	The key question is therefore how to prepare for AI advances\nand ensure that near-future Human-AI Teaming concepts of operation are both effective\nand safe. Aviation regulators such as the European Union Aviation Safety Agency (EASA), as\nwell as regulators in other safety-critical domains such as Oil and Gas [ 16], are well aware\nof this predicament, and EASA in particular have issued advance guidance for aviation\n‘Human-AI Teaming’ scenarios [ 17,18], depending on the level of autonomy of the AI under\nconsideration for implementation into flight operations.	Preamble	88	2	\N	\N	{}	[0.020738017,0.009730282,-0.05814215,0.01584655,0.04454277,0.03936226,0.038466148,0.040421337,-0.033572946,0.02815132,-0.022495056,-0.019372424,-0.05604159,0.017391454,0.035905346,0.010084118,0.031503383,-0.06642664,-0.10522535,-0.031002376,-0.00068827916,-0.033673868,-0.024389872,-0.0028414645,-0.056806237,-0.009428605,0.01757723,-0.03908768,-0.020374287,-0.0045407633,0.025692444,-0.08424716,0.034643836,0.014534881,-0.021079037,0.013959312,-0.00024485766,-0.030949773,0.0670278,0.0012727822,-0.05413908,-0.10891508,-0.030810587,-0.03274714,0.030869106,0.05441149,-0.04121369,-0.0109508755,0.013313138,-0.027481891,-0.020434596,-0.044319175,0.002677648,-0.09200682,0.01902193,-0.0025039248,0.032749623,-0.053615402,-0.033407565,-0.045710955,1.0369775e-05,-0.017768007,0.039416928,-0.005436014,-0.04361594,-0.0053465674,0.019882007,-0.00072530186,0.030571435,0.034185108,-0.010361955,-0.039787937,-0.03973936,-0.035666883,0.08009034,0.10229426,0.04538013,-0.048706867,0.050019216,-0.0874887,0.05846762,-0.004897143,-0.008968801,0.07782734,-0.014272529,0.046528313,-0.024517296,-0.029440532,0.027103042,0.05789379,-0.050334718,-0.060803205,0.094157636,0.015617027,0.088782065,0.10785589,-0.059612297,-0.015524676,-0.03816187,-0.029641706,0.04770144,0.011225232,0.016300643,0.0031787206,-0.051458813,0.019334994,0.0953197,-0.068779215,0.067354165,-0.06159462,-0.025542194,0.027502548,0.03964349,-