1190	9	54	For the supervision case, the primary goal of the supervisor is to verify that the CAGA system\nexecutes collision avoidance manoeuvring according to the COLREGs. That is, according to rule 8a,\ncollision avoidance manoeuvres should be executed using positive, timely, and actions with good\nseamanship. As mentioned in the baseline case, there are no explicit acceptance criteria for what\nconstitutes a manoeuvre with good seamanship, but it was clear that movements that clearly\ndemonstrate the vessel’s intention are central to this notion.	3. Results	82	3	\N	\N	{}	[0.01921141,0.03973536,-0.017859519,0.009960948,-0.018514428,0.009219932,0.01750126,-0.051029373,-0.016418774,0.027792832,0.080571584,-0.02342891,-0.03918631,0.11508848,-0.108564466,-0.0595144,0.022962958,-0.03809182,0.007458144,0.055960197,0.027339807,0.022270283,-0.051214274,-0.036957778,-0.16799174,-0.028085753,-0.02256612,-0.016484406,0.06886965,-0.029512865,0.010750789,0.030891204,0.029222498,0.0012964815,0.0058313855,0.0765345,0.042839207,-0.09859474,-0.077253446,0.036847055,-0.044890538,0.020710226,0.05315359,0.038307484,0.05171832,0.012663666,-0.022460613,-0.025124384,-0.057043385,0.0022395954,-0.06968486,-0.02258636,0.04134761,-0.014537143,0.016131232,0.009017598,-0.009531745,0.025783261,0.0010859387,-0.06827467,0.026761107,0.02967926,0.013054122,-0.016966116,0.04199998,-0.045974568,-0.04281435,-0.070571885,0.022117073,0.15645252,0.022451362,-0.084585495,-0.043152582,0.014602842,-0.017262148,-0.015960967,-0.012094529,-0.007240684,0.061452035,-0.07326055,-0.038290024,-0.04757866,-0.025517391,0.034888495,0.014933381,-0.04143325,-0.014376979,0.026565606,0.083861016,0.08273588,0.061324753,-0.08359875,0.023745107,-0.085931264,-0.037441313,0.0023236182,-0.09263967,0.034397155,-0.0071687233,-0.03306835,0.053638257,0.03900605,-0.030320162,0.03601195,-0.0030131256,0.026507573,0.018046588,-0.027593028,0.012311949,-0.008508595,-0.0063566347,0.116011135,-0.0019157918,-0.014386513,-0.034498613,0.0928