937	8	18	What does the existing body of Human Factors knowledge suggest we should focus\non for HAT systems?\n3. What are the Human-AI Teaming requirements arising from the gap between what\nwe have currently in HF requirements systems, and the challenges of future HAT\nconcepts of operation?\n4. Are the new HAT requirements fit for purpose, i.e., can they be used by project\nteams to identify new system design insights to safeguard and optimise human-AI\nteam performance? Future Transp. 2025 , 5, x FOR PEER REVIEW 5 of 40\nThe fourth, ﬁnal step sees the application of th e new requirements to the HAT use\ncases, to see if they result in novel insigh ts and design improvements that are convincing\nto the respective project teams. If this is so, then the new set of HAT requirements can\nserve as a preliminary approach for other future HAT systems evaluations, the require-\nments set to be updated as user experience and HF research evolve with respect to HAT\ndevelopment and implementation. Figure 2.	Preamble	171	6	\N	\N	{}	[-0.02236797,0.0654683,-0.005336384,-0.042025246,0.0974776,0.033389065,0.022669371,0.04057976,-0.07041501,0.054399595,-0.04733424,-0.037132617,0.0023244116,-0.009286277,0.041245814,-0.03425428,-0.0065630055,-0.07330083,-0.014445701,-0.067805536,0.02392576,-0.012117594,0.005898275,-0.03560749,-0.09778561,-0.018973876,-0.01085893,-0.05741435,-0.044730827,0.00095317536,0.021973114,0.0765762,0.10138531,-0.029084941,-0.049138855,0.1058433,0.119632535,-0.00042376306,-0.020761196,0.016339112,-0.09625468,-0.06567843,-0.05116038,0.010052891,0.086117595,0.04620955,-0.017992472,-0.046402346,-0.09975309,0.08473007,-0.060238432,-0.006273642,0.090573154,-0.0595159,-0.031183152,0.067706354,0.05790521,-0.017891446,-0.021143712,-0.020042744,-0.04839511,-0.07808712,-0.027856216,-0.019089779,0.10291254,-0.008376979,-0.047655504,-0.05308949,-0.025167756,0.035485364,-0.03735329,-0.053558752,-0.05657682,-0.09885492,0.03439182,0.045466192,-0.0096911155,-0.06890181,0.0441