984	8	65	For ex-\nample, in Figure 6, ISA signals that the take-o ﬀ ‘window’ for the KLM is now too small\ndue to the BAW’s increased speed, and so the BAW will land prior to the KLM take-o ﬀ\nand takes position ‘2’ in the strip (as indicated by the upward arrow in the bo ttom left\nhand corner of Figure 6).. The real-time assistance provided by ISA en sures timely and accurate forecast up-\ndates, allowing Tower Air Tra ﬃc Controllers (ATCOs) to manage the tra ﬃc ﬂow more\neﬃciently, with more ‘look-ahead time’ than cu rrently, as ISA can see further ‘upstream’. The bene ﬁts are improved decision-making, enha nced runway utilisation, increased op-\nerational e ﬃciency, and a safer and more streamlined air tra ﬃc ﬂow that reduces the need\nfor ‘go-arounds’.	Preamble	134	3	\N	\N	{}	[-0.0560676,-0.020503629,0.008345122,0.069260515,0.014177756,-0.03300784,-0.04861236,0.0048102103,0.00613316,0.033422556,0.054059476,0.04256159,-0.045548074,-0.034348547,0.0036215852,0.06858401,0.037827346,-0.06500442,-0.06957349,-0.015797801,0.03353246,-0.03435778,0.008064931,0.043059334,-0.060682233,-0.044267416,-0.013567063,0.03522653,0.093201555,-0.13997689,-0.057575766,0.12080721,0.0833846,-0.040051226,-0.08011545,0.0049667293,0.039573915,-0.003629066,0.026223999,0.00041754742,0.0053540105,-0.0546924,0.027841438,-0.02579962,0.021284504,-0.0064866752,0.055833038,-0.0107742455,-0.025914662,0.025759377,0.058441773,-0.05719053,0.025127316,0.019072829,-0.014604672,0.096893795,-0.08795767,0.020513045,0.0793018,0.0112368055,0.00068557623,0.03190866,-0.051994413,0.028934961,0.044893503,-0.04424522,-0.01446274,-0.043781713,-0.014226261,-0.012214335,-0.027843785,-0.046908084,-0.029235387,-0.021424152,0.08261843,0.044276703,0.06630353,-0.030153017,-0.029063426,-0.044116516,0.04402621,0.020895677,-0.05042025,-0.024367563,0.007758078,-0.03526675,-0.049284916,-0.062972546,0.085534826,-0.02019405,0.06968768,-0.07857619,-0.06706221,0.032219835,-0.013010716,0.023071202,-0.0054920265,0.009913843,-0.064