1006	8	87	This led to the study\nof mental workload (MWL), considering the task demands vs. human capabilities and\ncapacities, including problems of overload and underload [61,63]. SA and Mental Workload signalled a deepening of the focus on cognitive activities,\nrelating them in a measurable fashion to the actual cognitive work and operational context,\ndelivering viable metrics that could be measured in simulations or in situ.	Preamble	64	2	\N	\N	{}	[0.008834292,-0.00996644,-0.030926768,0.021578323,-0.036548175,-0.04260238,0.04988971,0.02136771,0.04985561,0.050623186,-0.051683016,0.01604946,-0.024480503,0.04296273,0.06576102,-0.021232767,0.039142188,-0.09094773,-0.06831669,-0.014079796,0.14257874,-0.058896165,0.01258773,0.03958855,-0.01021822,0.029498229,-0.11998873,-0.069442876,0.012136115,-0.0019756095,0.046545886,0.023795782,0.040241145,-0.0028934085,0.011506949,0.06023594,-0.013692109,0.0035494028,0.038867373,-0.01892124,-0.10229601,-0.057794396,0.039087832,0.083592795,-0.015220336,-0.027319599,-0.016971212,-0.067867644,-0.043503195,-0.007973336,-0.09233563,-0.017514046,0.038462408,0.0061314856,0.039721366,0.02204783,0.08871361,-0.05383051,-0.034496486,0.003566068,-0.13333161,-0.072168715,-0.009041804,-0.02532482,0.052602164,0.033349782,-0.03960018,-0.026888248,-0.07755528,-0.045047596,-0.018064313,-0.06700087,0.005339501,-0.012825878,0.054533184,-0.025258632,-0.06549448,-0.03942638,0.06346637,-0.05459833,0.07153201,0.032171227,-0.0060564503,0.019291228,0.042687073,0.0026335074,-0.0075078914,0.049855556,0.055615127,0.001084579,0.0100476695,-0.090577506,-0.04653353,0.0372288,-0.003343931,-0.05886407,0.014493128,0.061470937,-0.10726977,-0.015228626,0.029957226,0.0077806828,0.045693956,-0.010879406,-0.08387215,0.044064336,0.043506574,0.059763364,-0.034960695,-0.07111005,-0.06455571,0.0048385137,-0.0037170611,0.021922369,0.00022574764,0.017931508,-0.07105747,0.048869453,-0.016545093,0.043217674,0.03738594,-0.014443207,0.013666575,-0.03486656,0.022225734,-0.07185