1035	8	116	What we need is a way to determine\nwhen these and other AI ‘failure modes’ are likely, given the type of ML/LLM being used,\nits data, and the operational context it is being applied to. It is likely that a taxonomy of AI\nfailure mechanisms will develop as more experience is gained with AI-based systems, but\nit would be preferable not to have to learn the hard way. The second unknown, or ‘barely known’, relates to ‘human+AI’ failure modes, i.e., the\nlikely failure types when people are using and interacting with various types of AI tools. We already have ‘complacency’, but this is a catch-all term, and knowing when it is likely or\nnot, as a function of the human-AI system design, is unpredictable. This is problematic: how\ncan a safety-critical system be certified if complacency is a likely user characteristic and\nthe AI can fail?	Preamble	146	5	\N	\N	{}	[0.034984604,-0.13270234,0.008646078,0.0184731,0.08653152,-0.01908902,0.025695197,0.07175312,-0.058514398,0.016533291,-0.059176236,-0.06137668,0.06325784,-0.026214777,-0.007941337,-0.03657664,0.03633677,-0.019481426,0.002164162,0.005726119,0.033303123,0.02265837,-0.05888792,-0.016959788,-0.07064492,0.042304583,0.016842222,-0.047348734,-0.04202383,-0.030644603,0.03846281,0.0034390627,-0.014530335,-0.02018602,-0.00014343877,0.018211663,0.016860537,-0.006320436,0.06540216,-0.04693114,-0.0029477526,-0.06270865,0.00960099,-0.045167066,0.041746218,0.085760795,-0.032626227,-0.07604087,-0.06356841,0.016508048,-0.071497135,0.01890668,0.06859625,0.037235446,0.0073529235,0.009753097,0.03065668,0.09573836,-0.060078032,0.050299395,0.04103872,-0.032854885,4.6613135e-05,-0.021888824,0.10952729,0.095224306,-0.012782848,-0.036451504,0.021750733,0.051832896,-0.008953837,-0.04362281,-0.11214904,0.025853124,0.021146212,0.019045271,0.0035291107,-0.0500211,0.04117941,-0.036637776,0.010090715,0.07346138,-0.039977223,0.09548702,0.03679062,-0.0059086694,-0.03661696,0.022185965,0.038553704,-0.032896362,0.025004078,-0.0163069