1137	9	1	Despite previous research addressing human factors in\nautonomous shipping and remote control, few studies have focused on how to support the humans’\nmental processes in this new role. Therefore, this study performed a goal-directed task analysis\naddressing goals, decisions, and SA requirements for human-supervised collision avoidance. Data\nwas obtained from in situ observations and interviews with nine navigators onboard passenger\nferries, an appraisal of the collision regulations, and of relevant company documentation.	Preamble	72	3	\N	\N	{}	[0.09795755,-0.007890661,0.0018125704,0.0031873437,0.10619752,-0.056706436,0.0890524,0.009145106,-0.07869919,0.064308256,0.0015535731,-0.02965348,0.0027659228,0.08096875,-0.021620322,-0.008230204,0.0461856,-0.06804201,-0.110710494,0.018638993,0.0063810595,0.05199593,0.017144304,-0.006209327,-0.12305952,0.03823791,0.057930846,-0.07538524,-0.056697566,0.0020368581,0.02752396,-0.05107038,0.011880439,0.047386173,-0.013505071,0.020285698,0.001972569,-0.049959518,0.048006926,-0.07080582,-0.0823091,-0.078987285,0.0018511621,0.044017717,0.03420573,-0.024236422,-0.018940726,-0.096460454,-0.024161272,0.0020414258,-0.09247694,0.029467713,0.051621,-0.098315954,-0.049861275,-0.010319789,0.023407754,0.040003777,0.007272763,0.011111799,-0.016739663,-0.02080444,0.0019466726,-0.030005282,0.028254334,0.0054765004,-0.03333466,-0.03579984,0.038178865,0.06035784,0.024398895,0.032556944,-0.0035309521,-0.011518307,0.096907556,-0.032717146,-0.053222444,-0.018093538,0.007859472,0.0040627164,-0.036352683,-0.046791505,-0.02486744,0.110118344,0.036039904,-0.013827568,-0.010099459,0.12545277,0.01746641,0.08005177,-0.020616688,-0.15208286,0.092482954,0.031739347,-0.06466546,-0.008609445,-0.122041844,0.0091373045,-0.008819924,-0.037800796,0.01119261,0.030364385,-0.03641804,0.0433222,-0.024570132,0.019468274,0.018012946,-0.020982495,0.037594195,-0.038788114,-0.050529025,-0.018551474,-0.023477552,0.009799599,-0.09888698,-0.05468948,-0.004824673,0