1152	9	16	It\nmay be a challenge to envision an autonomous CAGA system designed to adhere to the rules whilst\nat the same time designed to break them (Miyoshi et al., 2022). One could consider setting boundaries for the autonomous system by defining when collision\navoidance responsibility is performed by the system and when it is performed by the navigator. This\nwould allow the system to operate autonomously within clearly defined limits and delegate\nresponsibility when it cannot perform its function to a sufficient degree.	1. Introduction	83	3	\N	\N	{}	[-0.025837874,0.017596126,-0.013331751,-0.051994424,-0.05883498,-0.09052283,-0.031755153,0.0066449544,0.014860708,0.031117337,0.001063638,-0.027593745,-0.023066398,0.062147584,-0.03547946,-0.06288112,0.021934481,-0.011147207,-0.07422099,0.025142008,0.07428151,0.03974343,-0.049059443,0.059881337,-0.18323351,-0.023199607,0.0010969962,-0.010533332,0.006252678,-0.09072943,0.031139454,-0.05588199,-0.011283678,0.022309987,-0.028329883,-0.001728753,-0.06675892,-0.08631804,-0.019647688,-0.07982487,-0.04079174,0.038452428,0.037735194,0.07019284,0.07857032,0.02884024,-0.01714963,0.013909605,-0.03262213,-0.068628944,-0.018483456,-0.058702435,0.02624878,-0.015809566,-0.022120465,0.005550046,-0.004613064,0.013695229,0.033225574,0.0058793086,0.022189716,-0.00049855356,-0.020156315,0.0025357394,0.00833505,-0.0106107,-0.062226865,0.021752618,-0.0063572936,0.13348524,-0.0052187964,-0.03468253,0.047083512,0.005778345,0.10102161,-0.020751934,-0.08738337,0.022801151,0.039275337,0.003335418,0.023360679,-0.06649225,-0.044234958,0.049275145,0.023467649,-0.03207547,-0.04329759,0.0105817905,0.12603688,-0.037636522,0.034426443,-0.022549262,0.116383635,-0.007579657,-0.011586266,-0.060181584,0.0028854758,-0.12664522,0.026058722,-0.038981907,-0.011774581,0.010883454,-0.012196092,0.031016571,0.012217749,0.044975143,0.019413384,-0.00011659928,-0.0053320546,-0.008416079,0.022861402,-0.005284032,0.06522719,0.0072238813,-0.06416214,0.049704913,-0