1149	9	13	Given these findings in the context of autonomous shipping, it becomes clear that further\nunderstanding is needed regarding the role of the human as a supervisor in autonomous collision\navoidance.\n1.3. Human-supervised collision avoidance\nCollision avoidance is internationally regulated through the collision avoidance rules and were\ndeveloped to provide the “rules of the road” for maritime traffic. The collision regulations12/20/25, 2:05 PM Supporting human supervision in autonomous collision avoidance through agent transparency - ScienceDirect\nhttps://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0925753523002710 4/37\n(“COLREGs”) came into force in 1977 and, although the rules have been amended several times\nsince, they do not consider autonomous ships (IMO, 1977).	1. Introduction	100	3	\N	\N	{}	[0.00993926,-0.047826454,0.0051225857,0.039512508,0.047535047,-0.07399054,0.030147653,-0.0057331496,-0.11856417,0.05068378,0.028906696,0.005247227,-0.036937058,0.10039089,-0.07713792,-0.0040324503,0.03396813,-0.047130264,-0.059766747,0.01324312,-0.060773104,0.03358174,-0.03544191,-0.014722668,-0.10770138,-0.009806768,0.050099958,-0.072708786,-0.042160846,-0.013066218,0.0009773525,-0.025074614,0.0670606,0.06206359,0.020955142,0.0023308252,0.062602036,-0.06366098,0.05712949,-0.008874798,-0.02264887,-0.05063559,-0.019945815,0.04125321,0.034882862,0.004379009,-0.0041125794,-0.085958295,-0.07344972,0.00064135925,-0.047285497,0.043809015,0.048637304,-0.037909295,-0.04271378,-0.052125692,0.02974238,0.045284804,0.021794885,-0.017416144,-0.019034212,-0.0071707633,-0.0068780812,-0.014858969,0.018451607,-0.07427386,-0.035488803,-0.048163943,0.029951364,0.076025754,0.021731323,0.04309265,-0.00047104573,0.023451773,0.092542954,-0.03726874,-0.0113219125,0.018465364,0.07600524,-0.025025923,-0.013807763,-0.069896065,0.05412935,0.031733382,-0.063072026,-0.051107544,-0.01695409,0.08733929,0.018831274,0.060934596,-0.019026028,-0.11832197,0.093144655,0.021619994,-0.11256219,-0.0