1159	9	23	As such, this study aims to establish an information basis for developing\nhuman supervised CAGA systems in the ship autonomy context.\n2. Method12/20/25, 2:05 PM Supporting human supervision in autonomous collision avoidance through agent transparency - ScienceDirect\nhttps://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0925753523002710 6/37\n2.1. Establishing a framework\nA Goal-Directed Task Analysis (GDTA) was performed to determine and describe the cognitive\nprocesses involved in collision avoidance (Endsley et al., 2003). Specifically, the goals, decisions, and\nSA requirements relevant for avoiding collisions were captured providing an understanding of how\ndecisions are made when ha ndling vessel collision situations (see Fig. 1).	1. Introduction	95	4	\N	\N	{}	[0.064143546,0.037866995,-0.042917784,0.01086885,0.046002794,-0.075196914,0.07124523,0.01018251,0.019839982,0.03778459,0.01139836,-0.06878278,-0.01243731,0.089837536,-0.037889194,-0.052562766,0.075595185,-0.046654068,-0.10975289,-0.017949082,0.047305793,0.043759383,-0.03991353,0.006187259,-0.13012065,-0.002683733,0.04062095,-0.08269014,-0.020458583,-0.0121099325,0.07621843,-0.05924637,0.022131223,0.04184534,-0.025787627,0.03635832,-0.030503593,-0.028705612,-0.016914442,-0.042186912,-0.10834303,-0.001165498,-0.000109038505,0.04733571,0.050498717,-0.004237711,-0.060306348,-0.10825323,-0.04902081,-0.0038875118,-0.12746201,-0.043207582,0.059945162,-0.061958965,0.0030624378,0.028624192,-0.0030217788,0.012541285,0.017950244,-0.03509634,-0.0040952438,-0.02119173,-0.026998587,-0.0038613216,0.014915246,0.027876163,-0.017853778,-0.017409699,0.01366381,0.006373862,0.01605198,0.03927463,0.013594173,-0.019363375,0.097592294,0.012686852,-0.061344873,0.013348836,0.06528572,-0.039130192,0.006763539,-0.022636348,-0.01479955,0.08696168,0.049867403,-0.001705186,-0.017043374,0.14535077,0.009423208,0.021804838,0.0028685357,-0.092888586,0.05644234,-0.00060635695,-0.030807894,0.039189998,-0.098164104,-0.026307553,0.