1165	9	29	In situ observations\nIn situ observations were performed of how potential collision situations were handled by\nnavigators on duty. The observations were performed whilst interviewing the navigators and were\nconveniently used as examples and objects of enquiry during the interviews. Therefore, potential\ncollision situations that arose during the visits were observed, noted, and discussed in detail.\n2.2.3. COLREGs\nAn appraisal of the COLREGs was performed to identify goals, decisions, tasks, and information\nneeds provided in the rule descriptions.	1. Introduction	78	4	\N	\N	{}	[0.0011398726,0.013583419,0.05212135,-0.00084242516,0.025552128,-0.107655555,0.033259127,0.07093553,-0.0566006,0.028029198,-0.015715964,-0.011231051,0.004726357,0.038588166,-0.07487255,-0.05343726,0.021902189,-0.018838322,-0.06598327,0.0650866,-0.030531354,0.006465388,-0.02388244,0.037002876,-0.07664337,0.01894165,0.010962708,-0.018225884,0.008565171,-0.019050878,-0.0014570161,0.09023146,-0.008174552,0.061196636,-0.027246188,0.06919206,0.077803776,-0.05246164,0.039153438,-0.017947352,-0.08273226,-0.037154175,0.072892055,0.029824248,0.010948291,0.0020405254,0.029414663,0.0031352383,-0.021198375,0.074231856,-0.094881706,-0.051628955,-0.007782737,-0.0199636,-0.0066419463,-0.0028264734,-0.0057157003,-0.09684657,0.036856778,-0.014430931,0.003190385,0.022906424,-0.036816157,0.058156807,-0.0039845193,-0.0032696577,-0.007880228,-0.039397538,0.062481705,0.07466657,-0.003257952,0.0034020331,0.0038330022,-0.030006936,0.0005099917,-0.014352829,-0.059747368,-0.02975994,0.025169587,-0.0733065,0.018417777,-0.023750287,-0.02361488,0.055407245,0.030418027,-0.07121114,-0.010255511,0.033951454,0.00991171,0.019045012,-0.0048602456,-0.09053685,0.024552424,-0.001267026,-0.02786699,0.039786946,-0.035657704,0.032154042,0.07384062,0.0007195238,0.040332533,0.030979505,-0.016236864,0.080118194,-0.11418726,0.008977335,-0.048664894,-0.09897626,0.013309828,0.011235752,-0.02039522,0.04682098,-0.01727053,0.014