1179	9	43	Rule 6: Safe speed\nRule 6 – Safe speed is described as “every vessel shall at all times proceed at a safe speed so that she\ncan take proper and effective action to avoid collision and be stopped within a distance appropriate to\nthe prevailing circumstances and conditions” (IMO, 1977). In determining safe speed, the na vigator\nshall consider several influencing factors that shall be taken into account such as the state of\nvisibility, traffic density, manoeuvrability, background lights, meteorological conditions, and\ndraught in relation to water depth. In addition, limitations of equipment, i.e., radar, shall be\nconsidered.	3. Results	98	3	\N	\N	{}	[0.020436767,0.044267144,-0.04998753,-0.050839968,0.05721078,-0.007018503,-0.0458912,-0.005832163,-0.101809636,0.05399158,0.036882672,-0.010471564,0.00174909,-0.010892309,-0.07228041,-0.045042686,0.04055641,0.034632687,-0.16614449,0.05396759,0.05227563,0.03134097,-0.00020156204,-0.028099742,-0.10509775,0.017259287,-0.0032669643,0.0028784822,0.029033676,-0.02739693,-0.073378645,-0.018309169,-0.059916526,0.044179384,-0.07981244,-0.051842194,0.02122225,-0.031948935,0.029379187,0.039085064,-0.06824949,-0.060379386,-0.008797678,0.032781027,0.05989945,0.032454886,0.0051172916,-0.021438753,0.044986703,-0.041901857,-0.05968483,-0.028404238,-0.012349032,0.016401974,-0.005107206,-0.033755425,-0.12701842,-0.04365675,0.028467024,0.019433534,0.035896286,0.022999454,-0.0040114634,0.0003319795,0.054215413,-0.042385187,-0.06723115,0.029514046,0.018019654,0.14547636,-0.038221903,-0.0011235359,0.043473348,0.0039641177,-0.047370818,-0.037468553,0.041193426,-0.033011537,0.0060850806,-0.075422525,-0.007170008,-0.06898416,0.031255115,0.00791738,0.030278945,0.0051372545,0.047518406,0.055844493,0.07892783,0.020490656,0.03505668,0.013905206,0.09119633,-0.06433849,-0.0034069782,0.020757042,-0.107946835,-0.05907059,0.019346356,-0.0055955113,0.043986734,-0.011888899,-0.021715088,0.1544294,0.025688091,0.023245368,0.03762262,0.08002628,