1195	9	59	The CAGA system continuously detects and analyses its\nenvironment in search for traffic conflicts, and subsequently makes decisions and executes\nmanoeuvres to avoid collisions whilst informing the human supervisor about its actions. As the\nsystem is not dependent on input from the supervisor to perform its actions unless deemed\nnecessary, this type of automation implementation requires a high degree of sophistication. The\nrole of the hu man has therefore changed from an active one to supervisory one that manages a\nsystem by means of exception (Cummings et al., 2007, Sher idan and Verplank, 1978).	4. Discussion	94	3	\N	\N	{}	[-0.022726433,0.022554304,-0.05519121,-0.01782686,-0.025755208,-0.032668147,0.11428425,-0.02240145,-0.009269023,0.017664146,-0.0018670558,0.005088842,-0.026512817,9.427564e-05,-0.039409835,-0.04923756,0.03393465,-0.07032118,0.04341364,-0.05953684,0.026956512,-0.0210427,-0.10154717,-0.0019891986,-0.17395353,-0.0639543,-0.03703814,0.020433934,0.003951666,-0.09890543,0.012982681,-0.02383419,0.10372977,-0.010244483,-0.0443101,0.0111884065,0.0008202048,-0.07470625,-0.04786333,-0.08441142,0.012866343,-0.025440859,0.018074589,0.036371067,0.00531955,-0.028813682,-0.06426817,-0.056157265,-0.028207246,-0.09574699,-0.07808888,-0.034484737,0.112944774,-0.0048130476,-0.0076273405,0.012938542,0.049216352,0.036176734,0.0032110799,-0.09777817,-0.02292318,-0.0008109127,-0.051092055,-0.004638525,0.07117959,-0.00081610953,-0.0066782576,-0.119242795,0.03385086,0.04917223,-0.031027792,-0.015612915,-0.055353645,0.03860113,0.04677865,-0.065171964,-0.039605815,-0.013169904,0.08469523,-0.043589797,0.044492446,-0.03574679,-0.078157924,0.098236755,0.056837358,-0.0020449928,-0.037689727,-0.0191822,0.08696847,-0.018055728,-0.015175109,-0.037333317,0.110820174,-0.039554697,-0.026257418,0.0031555733,0.00066175574,0.030886566,-0.0061049224,0.02543821,0.0418991,0.0005133029,0.008228916,-0.013641925,0.01861771,0.051767696,0.0098835435,-0.038500078,-0.019948052,0.0