1206	9	70	In determining which speed is safe given the\ncircumstances (rule 6), the system should provide the chosen safe speed, the parameters this is\nbased on, and any uncertainties in the sensor data affecting the chosen safe speed. In terms of\nestimating collision risk (rule 7), the system should show which vessels, in the short to long range,\nform a collision risk, including its understanding of vessel type, size, distance to target and the\npresence of a tow. Finally, in determining the collision avoidance manoeuvre (rule 8), the system\nshould show, amongst others, which actions it intends to perform, when it intends to perform these\nactions, including its understanding of vessel priorities, i.e., which ship will stand-on, and which\nship will give-way.	4. Discussion	121	3	\N	\N	{}	[0.04711332,0.046556573,-0.049918782,0.0025218856,0.07702047,-0.008812682,0.008012956,0.10333884,-0.09061711,0.047744557,0.023944754,-0.0014315774,0.009844691,0.011551913,-0.13102622,0.013690922,0.014802084,-0.017949251,-0.11850405,0.048007738,0.07089595,0.04308303,-0.0415416,-0.0517703,-0.13820638,-0.016184315,0.034772716,0.00016712939,-0.040435303,-0.049786817,-0.01809733,-0.032248795,0.03572127,-0.032356422,-0.014325054,-0.032007612,0.008017945,-0.116611026,0.03582722,0.032683,-0.07407681,-0.061037328,-0.008348141,0.05755126,0.08788499,0.017096015,-0.015893366,-0.021609291,0.03640149,0.02083318,-0.08676127,-0.030762913,0.006814722,0.029778548,0.03416286,-0.053686127,-0.09585162,-0.0025651704,-0.013292339,-0.026694264,0.039132547,-0.037986968,0.020041592,0.007979367,0.011585402,-0.03336485,-0.009563897,0.026479086,-0.038090907,0.13810445,0.021113707,0.037531782,-0.042174056,0.011931484,0.058623534,-0.02888352,0.007231237,-0.0023013926,-0.0039781327,-0.08192106,-0.0318907,-0.025068628,-0.031322144,-0.016760362,0.014112186,0.020533752,-0.05266904,0.10986516,0.111333705,0.04828877,0.004169835,-0.07763746,0.043271698,-0.024686724,-0.016247863,0.062081773,-0.10525517,-0.013557635,