1211	9	75	However, based on our results, acknowledging the study’s limit to\nrules 5 to 8 only, it is clear that care should be taken not to overload the user with information. Implementing transparency is “as much an art as it is a science”, and the potential for visual clutter\nand distraction should be considered as this may potentially offset transparency’s benefits\n(Wickens, 2018, p. 39). Presenting all information identified in this study, as depicted in Fig. 5, Fig. 6,\nFig. 7, Fig. 8, continuously is likely not prudent, and further work should focus on teasing out which\ninformation has precedent over other information and in which circumstances (see van de Mer we\net al., 2023 for preliminary results).	4. Discussion	117	3	\N	\N	{}	[0.044765264,0.026905522,0.033388413,0.028529072,0.10500959,0.018447928,0.0041756644,0.013871272,0.016008053,-0.012817435,-0.015760498,0.041774616,-0.02693622,-0.05956832,-0.02483926,-0.012505809,0.054354995,-0.03678466,-0.082554586,-0.06440213,0.0779045,-0.06514379,0.086246766,0.0038357242,0.029575441,-0.0094258,-0.0033574246,-0.082805924,0.023762997,-0.015295907,0.0018190496,0.008231985,0.045948584,0.0027738223,-0.0951154,-0.02298071,-0.023145879,0.058310963,-0.017711638,0.010267135,-0.030961232,0.0054120305,-0.012212475,0.080486484,0.026904512,-0.0107209105,0.02652773,-0.032541286,-0.04007393,-0.017170087,-0.1056518,-0.060531173,0.01979105,0.010992203,-0.031100098,-0.07301279,-0.019806957,-0.040886298,-0.07387325,0.035223268,-0.030211719,-0.012579462,-0.06945491,0.05123783,0.04431976,0.065436006,-0.0041399663,-0.036531083,-0.022068264,0.04118854,0.019198468,0.089192696,0.030364612,-0.005689117,0.015150629,0.036661718,-0.06284592,0.030876372,-0.025752379,-0.08030444,0.09397027,-0.051925007,0.021430282,0.0008809599,-0.025934527,-0.07162513,-0.04120383,-0.047828496,-0.10679404,0.008054603,0.015852083,-0.047468252,0.03208604,0.024068184,-0.021599324,0.0011625182,0.01786271,-0.046369944,0.028486038,0.026948694,-0.01776415,0.0395420