1227	10	8	Measuring Safety Culture\nThe EUROCONTROL Safety Culture Question nairecontains 48 questions linked to\neight safety culture ‘dimensions’:\n• Management commitment to safety\n• Collaboration and involvement\n• Just culture and reporting\n• Communication and learning\n• Colleague commitment to safety\n• Risk handling\n• Staﬀ and equipment\n• Procedures and training\nAn example of the style of output from such a survey is shown in Figure 2 for three\ntypical safety culture questionnaire items. In this example, the ﬁrst statement clearly\nreﬂects ‘positive’ safety culture, with a few who are neutral about the issue and a small\npercentage of dissenters. The second item ha s a large ‘neutral’ component; this can mean\neither that the respondents are not sure, or they do not see how it applies to their work\nenvironment, or they prefer not to say. Al though the surveys are always anonymous and\nconﬁdential, some participants remain cautious.	1. Introduction	150	4	\N	\N	{}	[0.09297492,0.020966846,-0.111743286,-0.0136898635,0.07484388,0.06002919,0.098619506,0.013420494,-0.03545783,-0.01872041,0.096800596,-0.10837764,0.07078373,-0.013682684,-0.03944267,-0.07921489,0.012202588,-0.04484255,-0.11316249,0.043936137,-0.0675069,-0.018367233,0.12806228,0.09029546,-0.10157027,-0.047197606,0.06041499,0.037379727,-0.0014547893,-0.010872233,-0.045007784,0.023677759,0.020739814,0.013404621,-0.009526567,-0.0045030387,-0.0064834715,-0.01805457,-0.014233823,0.026523488,-0.11784854,-0.101777844,0.015134928,-0.07202991,-0.01874885,0.01670088,0.013921737,-0.014238532,-0.061647218,-0.010402616,0.010223596,0.040319055,0.049115825,-0.03388495,0.04474106,-0.06978422,0.006062592,0.03847525,-0.068570174,0.047026046,-0.032776836,-0.03175808,-0.06671613,0.015018429,-0.011821321,0.032141797,-0.12808165,0.0028404007,-0.025683066,0.0108571965,-0.08119223,-0.09111182,0.025209615,0.0117811,0.0120770605,0.019500835,-0.008533865,-0.03484888,0.0033485915,-0.053045314,0.08775035,0.04195114,0.078849