1231	10	12	Measuring Safety Culture\nThe EUROCONTROL Safety Culture Questionnairecontains 48 questions linked to\neight safety culture ‘dimensions’:\nManagement commitment to safety\nCollaboration and involvement\nJust culture and reporting\nCommunication and learning\nColleague commitment to safety\nRisk handling\nStaff and equipment\nProcedures and training\nAn example of the style of output from such a survey is shown in Figure 2 for three\ntypical safety culture questionnaire items. In this example, the ﬁrst statement clearly reﬂects\n‘positive’ safety culture, with a few who are neutral about the issue and a small percentage\nof dissenters.	1. Introduction	91	2	\N	\N	{}	[0.09872654,0.009735673,-0.11419818,-0.035645675,0.060109947,0.053767335,0.07062438,0.023510806,-0.028515866,-0.012503709,0.10765321,-0.10723784,0.08364502,0.010969718,-0.049500868,-0.10235277,0.009623151,-0.030208299,-0.10838644,0.026364153,-0.045494016,-0.017412608,0.12960511,0.08510499,-0.14882445,-0.030810189,0.04772404,0.052958485,-0.00011893972,-0.012537575,-0.036288988,0.012570143,0.028396783,0.010394811,-0.011270869,-0.002281848,-0.015249298,-0.020328507,-0.007767651,0.038600303,-0.11530894,-0.08712831,-0.0014401779,-0.05473405,-0.011691631,0.02944773,0.010901448,0.0006041829,-0.03239205,-0.013795938,0.01291512,0.049445182,0.041618284,-0.043444697,0.05344123,-0.055698376,0.012654988,0.037629224,-0.07660491,0.041172955,-0.027800927,-0.00988349,-0.0712058,-0.007817427,-0.029305188,0.022106031,-0.121404916,0.033219837,-0.017683564,0.016188081,-0.08235929,-0.0779468,0.032865383,0.020191422,-0.01648572,0.03420825,-0.011811973,-0.021678848,-0.010968767,-0.051335607,0.07289948,0.003105981,0.061258987,0.07267126,0.012882907,0.015641028,0.025351968,0.019209675,0.0034584643,0.008901818,-0.06919411,0.025132122,0.089913905,0.007184896,0.022245126,0.032064553,-0.039369542,0.09119754,-0.036728017,-0.037661392,0.06064989,0.043790635,-0.04037113,0.065085344,-0.052233268,0.010670915,-0.018955378,0.017615