1281	10	62	Category 3A could also affect safety culture, as the human\nmay be too far ‘outside the loop’ to intervene effectively in time. The ‘lesser’ categories,\nincluding 1B and 2A, could impact safety culture, even positively, as they could augment\nthe degree of control the human has over safety. Rather than degrading or eroding safety,\nAI could therefore possibly enhance safety, offering new safety affordances. This important\naspect is returned to in Section 4.\n2.6.	1. Introduction	74	4	\N	\N	{}	[0.028438605,-0.022235082,-0.0265971,-0.044701695,0.10735795,0.041349605,0.004466471,-0.012565866,-0.04577842,0.021995392,0.04578068,-0.031544454,-0.0298436,-0.047234107,0.04413345,-0.018593105,0.062162906,0.06302013,-0.12714532,0.023027081,0.015466599,0.017352952,0.09091433,-0.0035436326,-0.15584205,-0.0015279754,0.0058176853,-0.004845375,0.029946584,-0.03880775,0.0070228274,0.021523548,0.05871242,0.01165451,-0.028635904,-0.0067471787,-0.0024155118,0.0021079849,0.028376944,0.04817236,-0.070542134,-0.0429892,-0.00028836852,-0.020731175,0.035510343,0.045710657,-0.07891907,-0.07662959,-0.031239755,-0.06457486,-0.025131006,0.044468928,0.013000748,-0.012873818,0.006221509,-0.04418244,-0.008724504,0.03034305,-0.0480539,0.07146771,0.008837067,-0.0026836959,0.042882696,-0.0019743154,0.09420074,0.00015959809,-0.08433353,-0.050197925,-0.0034657745,0.061639,-0.027315792,0.0166175,0.028327346,-0.03125895,0.025172157,-0.010613222,-0.017016204,-0.023933612,0.030189293,-0.09734155,0.055614147,-0.014097868,0.058914486,0.045547344,-0.020872945,0.017616987,-0.053849403,-0.06619282,-0.039277844,0.058614153,-0.010296919,-0.094762295,0.13730356,0.019544236,0.057721034,0.04374252,-0.06787578,-0.02852642,-0.018924633,-0.039120685,0.005836331,0.017456029,-0.06721088,0.06783525,0.0038848747,-0.022876723,0.024987124,-0.038760196,-0.021921655,0.047618154,0.013870523,0.011148675,0.010064461,-0.09291266,-0.038753226,0.024641251,-0.04367254,0.001818909,0.11513339,0.015407501,0.027329704,-0.028