1312	10	93	These results are backed up by a further study [ 46] of attitudes to ‘emotional’ AI. This\nstudy is oriented more towards societal impacts than industrial ones, i.e., generative AI\nor AGI more so than narrow AI applications. It adds certain potential cultural impact\nareas into the human-AI teaming landscape, since industries, particularly global ones like\naviation, are affected by diverse cultural norms. Key acceptance parameters for emotional\nAI were found to be loyalty (potential to erode existing social cohesion in the team), fairness,\nfreedom from harm, purity (concerns about ‘mental/spiritual contamination’ by the AI)\nand authority (impacts on the status quo).	1. Introduction	102	4	\N	\N	{}	[0.057750482,0.021658745,0.022130748,0.016649883,0.05475862,0.0070946487,0.048681132,0.017094966,0.039591216,-0.009776771,-0.010806365,-0.02185518,-0.008054803,-0.019482084,0.009912369,0.029345049,-0.024247918,-0.06943319,-0.087975666,-0.04000051,-0.043311648,-0.01707245,-0.07513813,0.016557548,-0.016182754,-0.0046354653,0.044395294,-0.008769174,0.0014972667,-0.000685673,0.0104397135,0.03851158,0.14036554,0.044587873,-0.01652995,0.014872894,-0.012586736,0.0050019966,0.014694969,-0.060189795,-0.0037177552,-0.09982688,0.03265581,-0.06637738,0.045963325,0.012771329,-0.02648927,-0.004741674,-0.020852802,-0.010562952,-0.104678184,-0.010012397,0.030258873,-0.024514988,0.052658666,-0.01849176,0.05079728,-0.0139355725,-0.018298127,0.034518633,-0.028793437,-0.022552505,0.07423638,-0.025550159,-0.01633797,-0.022383038,-0.0402796,-0.026084563,-0.033918496,-0.018114826,0.06705468,-0.01700008,-0.03699398,-0.031302657,-0.0041663013,0.08529224,-0.0027026404,-0.08766818,0.058695387,0.013388967,0.01643346,-0.016873546,0.00018974695,0.036963698,-0.025543662,-0.03990181,-0.02529528,-0.029046163,-0.006995475,0.16066904,-0.027537426,-0.06540279,0.09453293,0.012790279,0.05377524,0.061195742,-0.056274805,0.025231544,-0.077187315,-0.014006268,0.017326578,0.07308735,-0.07162528,0.03