1285	10	66	Consider the pilot who ignores advice from an AI in favor of their own judgement, and\nthen has an accident, but also the case wherein the pilot follows the AI’s advice which turns\nout to be unsafe, also resulting in an incident or accident. In both cases, it will be easy to\nblame the human user rather than the AI, yet this could be unfair (such a situation is called\na ‘double bind’ in psychology). Accountability (and justice) would require an adequate\nmeans of redress to discern whether the AI ‘made a mistake’.	1. Introduction	93	3	\N	\N	{}	[0.034744393,0.030175386,0.0017054026,0.021615563,0.028243504,0.049974337,0.054400854,0.07386907,0.019364225,0.100603424,0.065536216,0.015763922,0.016890917,-0.007615322,-0.03192929,-0.0083559,-0.019832479,-0.010851392,-0.047752436,0.027561925,-0.030541396,0.019306395,-0.011291632,-0.012524808,-0.08985692,-0.019229077,0.03355068,-0.048405062,-0.01768335,-0.0111916,-0.002551134,-0.022539986,0.024450557,0.042421088,-0.0890678,-0.06507826,-0.042370673,0.035465684,0.04104134,-0.011849623,-0.004383243,-0.01735721,-0.03644471,-0.023430057,-0.010406376,0.05747898,0.012012778,0.004738017,0.018844903,-0.051110104,-0.10816409,0.020872034,0.03297556,-0.04054344,0.005896933,-0.026235813,0.022397121,0.12004174,-0.022222076,0.018484354,0.03222279,-0.036712218,-0.017887803,-0.005169247,0.123381786,0.10207124,-0.04286896,-0.081061915,0.0069918195,0.044456966,0.059212137,0.038136758,0.06158317,-0.02513129,-0.028323473,0.056590233,-0.007252584,0.0033829028,0.063636966,0.010151394,-0.0077865897,-0.007598246,-0.018402457,0.036493856,0.018371908,-0.027682325,-0.036567576,0.0007928093,0.11870462,0.0022403863,-0.056158677,-0.07455947,0.14754787,-0.04568423,0.039816774,0.0840628,-0.025986696,-0.007959759,-0.0909544,-0.010612942,0.03374488,0.043924876,-0.07578696,0.0052202316,0.06732367,0.07705767,0.06579058,-0.108917,0.0040288614,0.0014331164,-0.040542215,0.024711007,0.022551617,0.0037249133,0.07544246,0.009839387,-0.0073086107,0.0980673