1328	10	109	At the outset of this paper, it was noted that organizations need both an SMS (safety\nmanagement system) and safety culture. There is a very real danger that the potential safety\nimpact of integration of future AI ‘tech’ into operational aviation systems is underestimated,\nif it is believed current SMSs can handle such a transition. This would effectively be the ‘old\nwine in new bottles’ approach and could lead to signiﬁcant safety vulnerabilities emerging\nin future aviation systems.	1. Introduction	78	3	\N	\N	{}	[-0.0023223723,-0.01397436,-0.05073511,-0.055169906,0.040054884,-0.0036879685,0.07154575,0.061705355,-0.044501867,0.042892337,0.026192423,0.020536847,0.07725268,0.0047859615,0.0055226693,0.014994586,0.008507671,-0.10980433,-0.07101179,-0.009978645,-0.014732673,0.07407143,0.004527403,0.08296294,-0.087557286,0.04142227,0.01469745,0.012960036,-0.021086924,-0.0039437693,0.0021755088,0.048488718,0.056364715,0.07209318,-0.06933486,-0.061933566,0.011264266,-0.028562749,0.065621726,-0.03945236,-0.094278656,-0.08987078,-0.0577829,0.048165925,0.011802307,0.030981995,-0.011464432,0.013492631,1.0712871e-05,0.020635057,-0.027248325,-0.041658256,0.06479595,-0.04799905,0.010488171,0.003349279,0.033337157,0.0473918,-0.049073506,0.0020764465,0.013915734,0.029300895,0.009224022,0.027407333,0.0040133973,0.054821614,-0.08664698,0.028095258,0.038861867,-0.021711275,-0.026030576,-0.038205586,0.0005336981,0.058053575,-0.034658235,0.06395482,0.013766689,-0.019751804,-0.02326025,0.0342041,0.036810543,-0.036266018,0.0024601556,0.0550614,-0.024554564,0.04343489,-0.0515085,-0.005907067,0.017514545,-0.011125353,-0.052891478,-0.06607586,0.15884556,0.026331635,0.05181487,0.03166145,-0.062262192,-0.050360367,-0.029446904,-0.013667362,0.011629192,0.05300252,-0.0033581464,0.037567265,-0.042017702,0.046935756,0.068059705,-0.060551435,0.05737355,-0.0295476,-0.011754751,0.03351237,0.04621924,-0.10870164,-0.05635083,-0.021103188,-0.10339001,0.040682327,0.055229325,0.045477968,-