1387	10	168	Safety management systems (SMS)—the key counterpart of safety culture in\naviation—the SMS—will also need to adapt to higher levels of AI autonomy, as\nis already being suggested in [ 31,33]. This will probably require new thinking and\nnew approaches, for example with respect to the treatment of human-AI teaming in\nrisk models, rather than simply producing ‘old wine in new bottles.’ SMS maturity\nmodels, such as those that are used in air trafﬁc organizations around the globe [ 52],\nwill also need to adapt to address advanced AI integration into operations. Future Transp. 2024 ,4 376\n3.	4. Results	97	3	\N	\N	{}	[0.0075017875,-0.055142365,-0.046896182,-0.034572717,0.037949868,0.0035282343,0.038689874,0.07244687,-0.03586757,0.04365949,0.05729822,0.0015931933,0.053298447,0.029657206,0.032421444,0.019068552,0.022014743,-0.10444567,-0.103691444,-0.04227039,0.011576347,0.066592865,-0.0052508623,0.038923025,-0.06528799,0.0057403925,-0.011010097,0.017367167,0.00207744,-0.0100377565,0.022606546,0.04575965,0.09194172,0.04589443,-0.074531175,-0.030469729,-0.049700454,-0.036529735,0.042993017,0.008687209,-0.083057754,-0.08711649,-0.021403307,0.0023222559,0.040213045,0.0052239764,-0.061137404,0.0021514995,0.0009061168,0.012433481,-0.053113148,-0.012989512,0.028203355,-0.036706742,0.022841526,-0.0038067622,0.017712533,-0.017498434,-0.06065881,-0.002216209,0.015556322,0.007971472,-0.006988101,0.008273785,0.012121051,0.028256519,-0.053522658,0.039909445,0.026575673,0.008469447,-0.047287736,-0.06731058,-0.022903716,0.040428787,-0.0070853434,0.06759096,0.039899196,-0.055162173,0.006039585,-0.011091943,-0.009322548,-0.01779322,0.05268328,0.051908687,-0.028271392,0.024277827,-0.03363018,0.0005896446,0.025247438,0.031116826,-0.039077055,-0.043437798,0.122073755,0.038102407,-0.003216148,0.078792825,-0.07303987,-0.057391293,-0.027188262,-0.018228136,-0.017751506,0.038473014,-0.01712048,0.02258383,-0.04627382,0.004111137,0.08796609,-0.04696017,0.04890613,-0.019622201,-0.013