1400	11	3	Within this guidance,\nlevel 1 describes assistance functionalities to human operators. Level 2 describes applications of Human-AI Teaming. An\nadditional split was introduced for level 2A and level 2B\napplications. Levels 2A and 2B refer to the cooperation and\ncollaboration between humans and AI, respectively, outlining\nthe differences in authority and task allocation. The distinction\nbetween levels 2A and 2B is relevant for achieving different\ngoals requiring different kinds of interactions. While level\n2A (Human-AI cooperation) contains systems in which the\nAI-based system works to help the end user accomplish their\nown goal, AI-based systems on level 2B are designed to work\ntogether to achieve a predefined shared goal through a co-constructive approach [2]. Consequently, level 2B refers to an\nalmost equal relationship between humans and AI. Developing\nAI-based systems for this paradigm shift from systems with\nclear hierarchical relationships to systems with an almost equal\nrelationship between humans and AI is one of the big tasks\nof research and development for AI-based systems [4].	Preamble	165	7	\N	\N	{}	[-0.04828944,-0.008622365,-0.021988813,-0.05469277,-0.011377243,-0.030933833,0.02101884,0.03776434,-0.0040554786,-0.026672455,-0.061726164,-0.056083385,0.052922525,0.012824259,0.08269287,0.0223244,0.0363547,-0.0674307,-0.056011375,-0.03911817,0.052655913,-0.012947676,-0.010787373,-0.021775588,-0.096137755,-0.030156072,0.0094445,-0.044356413,-0.027184835,-0.007404522,0.056646153,-0.03456412,0.08660585,-0.018735617,-0.103186026,0.02923085,0.06410768,-0.009095405,-0.0020421005,-0.032110848,-0.09743288,-0.04820131,-0.054022413,-0.010874488,0.014193019,0.06994588,-0.045296386,-0.037177302,-0.06728995,-0.01709398,-0.07702611,0.003973236,0.010600733,0.014140817,0.07332701,0.13042594,0.020580761,0.04494604,-0.005234664,-0.015181899,-0.048857428,-0.024680898,0.0006096605,-0.014235,0.07240504,-0.020920437,-0.04528736,-0.00023914887,-0.0015263401