1422	11	25	This is\nin line with the requirements for explainability and acceptance\nof AI identified by previous work [27]. C. Conflict Detection and Conflict Resolution\nAn important part of the work of ATCOs is the detection\nand resolution of conflicts between flights in the monitored\nsector [28]. For this, the traffic is constantly monitored for\ndeviations from planned flight trajectories in position, speed,\nand flight level. The comparison between actual and plannedvalues for these parameters can be easily carried out by an\nautomated system, respectively a digital ATCO if the planned\ntrajectories are updated regularly. The development of methods\nfor a reliable calculation of conflicts is an important research\ntopic in the area of air traffic control, especially for long\nand medium-term forecasts. It is oftentimes combined with a\nprobabilistic approach [29] and 4-D trajectories [30].	Preamble	135	6	\N	\N	{}	[0.0055685975,-0.049754728,-0.061750047,0.005554235,0.029965062,-0.0055730985,-0.001250176,-0.015561705,0.069232434,0.047668923,-0.08888988,0.022600489,-0.023628604,-0.009850397,-0.071459286,0.019502006,-0.06826971,-0.04960981,-0.04326279,-0.048884064,0.048378192,0.017883506,-0.057793,0.03262921,-0.013273666,-0.01983583,0.03662019,0.010022947,-0.04894374,-0.023632092,0.037274513,0.019527182,0.03076046,0.011150493,-0.070630446,-0.036268193,-0.043947503,0.03031379,0.08661077,-0.060207997,-0.0071022804,-0.036194555,0.05954344,-0.025113508,-0.03483098,0.037490286,-0.057348005,0.08411781,-0.04579279,0.06456437,-0.0746933,-0.022404872,0.027837962,-0.04821453,0.057633583,0.04391272,-0.007434854,0.024757478,-0.01617954,0.0057186093,-0.08606354,0.024718162,-0.051714726,-0.010858245,-0.04963487,0.06200304,0.033658717,0.04930843,0.014353406,0.06416653,-0.032989863,0.07223199,0.0044810753,0.034568597,0.045968745,0.09886026,0.019623637,0.027828481,0.0035413601,-0.07982051,0.022893667,-0.006620179,-0.093062095,0.024557179,0.09452477,-0.06774989,0.024616743,0.0581