1423	11	26	In workshops with ATCOs [26], CD&R was identified as a\ncrucial task when talking about support from a digital ATCO to\nreduce the workload. For Human-AI Teaming the controllers\nproposed an implementation of the conflict resolution task\nwhere several solutions are created by the digital ATCO\nand presented to the human ATCO for selecting the most\nappropriate and implementing it manually. This requires a\nconflict resolution tool that is capable of adapting trajectories\nto several preferences defined by either the human operator\nor the digital ATCO, such as short trajectories, reaching the\nsector boundary in time, capable climb and descent rates, or\nsticking close to the original trajectory. Furthermore, the used\ncontroller working position has to be able to present several\nsolutions for a conflict and allow the ATCO to select the\npreferred one if this is not done automatically by the digital\nATCO.	Preamble	144	4	\N	\N	{}	[-0.04790003,-0.011748821,-0.0743838,-0.013536105,-0.01104408,0.022339975,0.016230362,0.029093219,0.014217017,0.076802745,-0.054009542,0.023165757,0.005693185,-0.030893592,0.029812701,0.018925166,0.010913553,-0.020269027,0.03171288,0.0050775846,0.06897086,-0.04500307,-0.050109442,-0.018351492,-0.08619334,-0.041806594,-0.019591516,-0.03928829,-0.028101077,-0.043141767,0.0021981716,0.03983121,0.048889123,-0.012629562,-0.05011415,0.028338207,-0.051939134,0.040505446,-0.000471622,-0.13636984,-0.02094739,-0.028610606,0.063965864,-0.060685582,0.0110049145,0.07156695,-0.0681558,0.06805068,-0.021363163,-0.0002618557,-0.011912075,-0.016905678,0.05605171,-0.010817668,0.025257168,0.089055024,0.03132005,0.057895966,0.008438145,0.027074303,-0.008083919,-0.023071235,-0.053070683,0.003811978,0.041672673,-0.004219658,0.037096944,0.037181016,-0.034053918,0.0015886388,0.032250073,-0.0018453416,0.06112555,-0.011065189,0.10431033,0.038454503,-0.017460108,-0.0026868265,0.07068931,-0.08041649,-0.02379581,0.0770354,-0.050294366,0.022569079,0.01004163