1419	11	22	SCOs, which are analogous to Single Pilot Operations\n(SPOs) in the cockpit [23], present a potential solution to\naddress staffing issues as well as capacity limitations. Unlike\nthe occasional use of a single ATCO, the SCO concept\nenvisions the planned deployment of one ATCO per sector. The DLR [8], [9] has proposed an SCO concept that combines\nthe tasks of radar and planner ATCOs into one role.	Preamble	67	3	\N	\N	{}	[-0.009578001,-0.052333888,-0.11649863,-0.014839364,0.022827227,-0.023913968,0.02808765,0.001299825,-0.06822595,0.036379173,-0.046031572,0.058816735,-0.020119479,0.021654826,0.052978117,-0.0074607693,0.037267283,-0.09884754,0.030293409,0.0137844095,0.033571012,-0.020986998,-0.097314455,0.09852435,-0.050041296,-0.08480139,-0.0111857345,-0.039344545,-0.09666889,0.009683361,0.013209539,0.12441212,0.04689112,0.029368252,-0.031653117,-0.006422094,0.038658503,0.076118134,-0.0032529994,-0.10308094,-0.036767796,-0.017014157,-0.038608138,0.0014179827,-0.038963586,-0.017694686,-0.04288839,0.011941787,0.021799173,-0.04269432,0.02907808,-0.083581656,-0.0033835815,-0.019995004,-0.025866013,0.07043447,-0.10104262,-0.01689978,-0.0060398816,-0.070463486,-0.0744128,-0.027647024,0.018480808,0.07165843,0.092459604,0.0052317525,0.04433769,-0.048033528,-0.056467257,0.001889479,0.0076759937,-0.064262986,0.05271372,0.014094017,0.061537303,0.008526022,0.02467142,0.03439089,0.07620625,-0.08637061,0.027099652,0.03237239,-0.09270741,-0.006288445,-0.026623195,-0.010022379,-0.051411133,-0.014201838,0.06114773,-0.000858252,0.037201688,-0.057564307,0.040849686,-0.07770115,-0.053227253,-0.004671802,0.02990501,-0.023261538,0.013226371,-0.018254232,0.03970426,-0.0034553914,0.05560939,-0.019402208,-0.01660196,-0.002847795,0.042796373,-0.10663388,0.020574467,-0.0055954554,-0.019234398,0.10413866,0.006136596,-0.059918627,-0.061926454,0.028032307,-0.12931749,0.038587924,0.044231888,0.04165194,-0.028970638,-0.07733823,-0.00687994,0.01728445,0.087434664,-0.03309258,0.003984798