1427	11	30	Especially in domains\nwhere safety is of critical importance, the trust of the users in\nhuman-technology interactions is of vital importance [33]. In\nline with Lee and See [34], trust of human teammates in their\ndigital teammate is defined as the “attitude that the digital\nagent will help achieve an individual’s goals in a situation\ncharacterized by uncertainty and vulnerability”. This means\nthat trust plays a fundamental role [35] when the human is\nuncertain that their teammate will perform competently and\nreliably (uncertainty) and when risks are tied to the teammate’s\nperformance (vulnerability).	Preamble	93	3	\N	\N	{}	[-0.018253373,0.034693073,-0.086799525,-0.10153654,0.008808929,-0.02084978,0.11940647,0.02975801,0.037379745,0.019007282,0.042705294,0.001703982,0.13613333,0.00026996466,-0.006035723,-0.04435645,0.0137036955,-0.018279918,-0.114751235,0.010942023,-0.063808925,-0.063467726,-0.046418156,-0.032353695,-0.07400679,-0.080897324,-0.008191474,0.012852857,-0.05600693,-0.059426963,-0.030881977,-0.022488242,0.0541253,0.010660764,-0.06224668,-0.012288206,-0.004787025,0.0027253288,-0.025514761,-0.049934026,-0.08494942,-0.10188346,0.02482849,0.042412113,-0.047295086,0.014291994,0.012064548,-0.048121154,-0.04050163,0.00046169612,-0.12462818,-0.025856882,0.00042123132,0.007875722,-0.023441484,0.014934711,0.046690095,0.015925502,-0.021371283,0.013188695,0.06374644,-0.050611276,-0.013610188,0.05887374,0.072672956,0.058193095,-0.0020304844,-0.05430745,-0.02573729,-0.0035443858,0.008997664,-0.0317963,0.0032969064,-0.04036088,0.0030348238,-0.04750151,0.01259526,-0.052354734,0.07464236,0.025804993,0.045243755,0.032583535,-0.013280898,0.02860992,-0.07454772,0.005592645,-0.008158185,-0.06808061,0.022365214,-0.0385349,-0.028451594,0.013354765,0.03759966,0.06801958,-0.0034773936,0.030723367,-0.019797215,-0.012718689,-0.07285397,0.013887519,0.0056253895,-0.0076066093,-0.063915335,-0.015758196,0.05773523,0.017196633,0.05019904,-0.03428101,0.025189072,0.016