1428	11	31	By having integrated automation in aviation some decades\nago, the human operators in ATC are supervising many aspects\nof the system and are being assisted by automated functionali-\nties, which change the role of the human in a system. There are\na large number of studies on the consequences of automation\non human operators [32], [36]. With the introduction of\nAI-based systems as a form of highly capable automation\ndirected at highly perceptual and cognitive tasks [32], the\nsame psychological phenomena occur as with\nconventional automation of Human-Technology interaction,\nas well as new ones. To sum up, people’s ability to oversee\nand interact with automation systems to maintain operational\nsafety [37] is negatively affected when switching from\nautomation on the level of information processing to the\nlevel of decision-making when actions are to be implemented\nbased on collected information automatically [38].	Preamble	141	4	\N	\N	{}	[0.013815053,-0.032197107,-0.02827553,0.004605572,-0.020602174,-0.011050519,0.105196424,0.051344253,-0.026663685,0.0621146,-0.014314864,0.012976384,-0.017382361,0.01787127,-0.009493963,-0.009513892,0.06169275,-0.11874169,-0.09456035,-0.013028975,0.004474377,-0.0017544861,-0.006090489,0.041013237,-0.061158888,-0.044303305,-0.014782834,-0.056729734,-0.035673648,0.009675353,0.02899888,-0.038941666,0.15590946,0.02327868,-0.04624811,-0.06572978,0.027883697,0.044096313,0.07147775,-0.13968287,-0.078593776,-0.1310804,-0.051543288,0.024786428,-0.014430292,0.055622183,-0.061446775,-0.07493379,-0.0031268047,0.034241453,-0.12357825,0.046058662,0.057826538,-0.08583107,-0.014967011,0.022748137,0.06269001,0.046110354,-0.009050359,-0.008060355,-0.03814537,-0.0051784706,-0.0028029766,0.04083615,0.03923694,0.035622515,-0.0286269,-0.105414286,0.067282826,-0.013980137,-0.0044844113,0.011475425,0.04125354,0.028822398,0.060575742,0.007360184,-0.053896446,-0.06307042,0.022423692,-0.0338138,0.027734548,-0.01330844,-0.043972593,0.07043151