1439	11	42	For example, Figure 3 depicts the conflict detection\nand resolution process. DIRC receives and analyzes conflict\ndetection information from the Trajectory Conflict Checker\n(TCC), which will be explained in Subsubsection III-A 1. Based on the analysis, it selects a flight from the conflict\npair and calls the Trajectory Generation and Advisory Tool\n(TraGAT), which is explained in Subsubsection III-A 2, to\nprovide solutions to resolve conflict. The solution received\nfrom TraGAT is then displayed to human ATCO with the\noption to accept or ask for another solution.	Preamble	87	4	\N	\N	{}	[-0.091557354,-0.06369815,-0.070745386,-0.010612694,0.06274149,-0.045070626,-0.01782999,-0.01539889,0.059163917,0.026820749,0.02577977,0.006670632,-0.021802405,-0.026725095,-0.0790302,-0.017827524,0.00600656,-0.05555471,-0.0037677905,-0.08434967,0.014200769,0.04395274,0.0131995715,0.01491068,-0.09594337,-0.017203497,-0.022818552,0.0023513366,-0.0017231831,-0.05328061,0.054597866,0.09896323,0.030421838,0.040446147,0.009280778,0.04275911,-0.030423904,0.015600104,0.04392198,-0.08878591,0.0035905067,-0.0064926115,0.006764922,-0.014780226,-0.010818418,-0.034431797,-0.0817779,0.040095877,-0.056031153,0.019768594,-0.060179137,-0.0020607512,-0.025015617,0.02949885,0.03137865,0.09375135,0.044362623,0.019900126,0.03472814,0.04897141,-0.03619438,0.016274365,-0.12625019,0.016261429,0.099227846,-0.0049375864,0.029744266,0.076631844,0.07079463,0.015173368,-0.018905206,0.032202367,0.015942391,0.03162607,0.018013433,0.069496,-0.043402743,0.022089502,-0.014379751,-0.17475784,0.018320262,0.026248908,-0.019593239,0.042826083,0.051881816,-0.022775315,0.034104936,0.0030418471,0.07127148,0.04374117,0.0078066215,-0.047286358,0.09785104,-0.021197502,-0.08800069,0.05275426,0.012648254,0.04395687,0.09942145,0.00025266205,0.059196893,-0.06285514,0.008810884,-0.04482486,-0.032696,-0.049560457,-0.005439965,-0.057965092,0.057679247,0.02231751,-0.08416793,0.009851507,-0.03729566,-0.04913009,-0.01798