1444	11	47	If the route structure is selected, the evolutionary\nalgorithm tries to use the standard climb and descent rates\nproposed by BADA data [43] and penalizes sharp angles\nbelow 90° or too many turns. The solution depends deeply on the additional data included\nin the request, for instance, other flights, route networks,\nbeacons for the observed sector, or restricted areas due to\nmilitary flights and environmental issues such as contrails. An\nexample is shown in Figure 4, with the original trajectory\nwith conflicts in red and the conflict-free solution in green.	Preamble	90	3	\N	\N	{}	[-0.03819713,0.002345462,0.017253457,0.030355655,0.00441808,-0.01848585,-0.09812579,0.04405906,-0.054786913,0.069591366,0.016325315,-0.013467629,-0.04028891,0.03107709,0.011094267,0.073866196,-0.043081243,0.03592255,0.012506567,-0.07690648,0.048741948,0.031557318,0.006681038,0.026903043,-0.116921805,-0.02147003,0.044314265,0.027022079,0.04664117,-0.0735237,0.049568128,0.07379064,-0.018235512,0.030712314,-0.05443617,0.009051846,-0.1449174,-0.02483123,0.024665622,0.047359683,-0.023140233,0.07596841,0.018621486,0.020014662,0.04988165,-0.018448796,-0.036108382,0.07542685,-0.008141585,0.01814393,-0.05130426,-0.03936599,-0.04268206,-0.011297598,0.070855476,0.03757616,-0.054544024,-0.018268539,0.030438198,-0.033578955,0.07961457,-0.080467746,-0.04064716,-0.0904975,0.013402509,0.014230358,-0.027081432,-0.030125538,0.018416252,0.023395326,0.021306675,0.02711465,-0.018425018,0.01123219,0.027557187,0.059407696,0.053881593,0.098302156,-0.080798596,-0.12432168,0.023851953,-0.005886182,-0.054501753,0.08668576,0.084234335,-0.058967136,-0.029301003,-0.06563509,0.12613158,0.08887119,0.039687086,0.039986346,0.025341112,-0.035305038,-0.022625474,0.07225347,-0.023533711,-0.072365284,-0.015659977,0.017593363,0.022598173,-0.06478854,-0.03682887,0.11241811,0.08205018,-0.023161532,0.057862315,-0.030882943,-0.0012562465,0.026562134,-0.032550927,0.062324595,0.021746993,-0.053202458,-0.08707029,-0.0