1469	11	72	For the scenario modeling, the following terms and defini-\ntions are defined [46], [47]:\n•Scene: “is describing a snapshot of the environment\nincluding the scenery and dynamic elements at a given\npoint in time”\n•Situation: “is the entirety of circumstances, which are to\nbe considered for the selection of an appropriate behavior\npattern at a given point in time”\n•Scenario: “is describing the temporal development be-\ntween several scenes in a sequence of scenes. Each\nscenario starts with an initial scene”\nFurthermore, the scenario definition based on [46], [47] is\nused. Therein, logical scenarios serve as a representation of\nmultidimensional parameter spaces of all included attributes. Concrete scenarios are a sub-set of a logical scenario, con-\ntaining a specific set of parameters that can be used as an\ninput for the simulation environment. In this paper, four concrete scenarios are shown. All are\nlocated in the sector Celle at medium traffic density.	Preamble	152	6	\N	\N	{}	[0.009244697,-0.0070364266,0.009393355,-0.048251066,0.05260697,-0.021565227,0.008530867,0.023947023,0.033700693,-0.036923762,0.022182293,-0.122904815,0.055894777,0.022870136,0.05541989,-0.034249745,0.03206177,-0.016072625,-0.050312925,0.07718295,0.060748287,-0.039401237,-0.07305598,-0.036288597,-0.07925675,0.036127113,0.079508044,-0.0003282612,-0.023687456,-0.02860868,0.05126855,0.10371255,-0.013956862,0.023400502,0.055353433,0.07519697,-0.087553,-0.053756204,-0.030105839,0.031126937,-0.0600168,-0.06618486,-0.011243339,-0.011754642,0.072690986,-0.010247029,0.042278986,-0.027000327,-0.04252754,-0.05675194,-0.076596566,-0.0032833484,0.007886627,0.009926754,0.03287786,-0.021600392,-0.0014862071,-0.016217703,0.033158176,-0.028080221,-0.017118474,0.032825142,-0.015498533,0.04941166,0.035767697,0.033409834,-0.07965701,0.048067257,0.05890666,0.0009245156,-0.033661272,0.04811756,-0.054484468,-0.08576929,-0.012079616,0.060226325,0.020311587,-0.03681927,-0.026748724,-0.10560304,0