1472	11	75	Especially, defining\nthe correct hierarchical structure, defining certain interrelations\nbetween the attributes also called ontology, and defining\nrelative constraints, as shown in Figure 6, were achieved in\nthe refinement process. For the simulation, three parameters of\nthe ATC ODD were identified as highly important to monitor\nfor the chosen scenarios.\n1)Attribute: Entry/Exit conditions of certain flights into\nneighboring sectors according to the flight plan\n2)Constraint: Minimal horizontal separation between two\nflights of 5 NM\n3)Constraint: Route deviation in terms of increased trajec-\ntory length of 1 NM and a maximum heading change\nof 20°\nOut of several executed scenarios, two were handpicked for\ndemonstration purposes of ODD violations during runtime. As described in Subsubsection III-B 4, the sector Celle was\nused for the simulations. Figure 7 shows the initial scene at\nt= 0 s with the aircraft EJU64TH and KLM1613 on a conflict\ncourse, where the black lines indicate the current trajectories. The trajectory section marked in red, indicates the area of the\npredicted closest point of approach (CPA). In the left upper\ncorner, the table highlights DRICs information on the conflict,\nsuch as involved aircraft marked in yellow, time to CPA,\nminimal separation, and flight level.	Preamble	197	6	\N	\N	{}	[-0.002762704,-0.042179395,-0.049876325,-0.027515013,0.059051767,-0.012884579,-0.10566719,0.005492678,0.0036303564,0.044516414,-0.009825924,-0.043847114,0.009149275,-0.017271236,-0.00824065,0.008922819,0.010274445,-0.079930924,-0.103412405,0.034302697,0.09900583,0.0007455869,-0.018767977,0.037976317,-0.07195355,-0.023080735,0.0018786356,0.0486779,-0.030622736,-0.0799636,0.05539225,0.09381679,-0.028505117,0.026795326,0.04825001,0.019314686,-0.0062985728,-0.011736689,0.01360729,-0.019152509,-0.06629163,0.029095344,0.02997107,0.047620915,0.04702305,0.046624012,0.0027593442,0.0012815373,-0.062597655,0.0032218967,-0.057676364,-0.03410985,-0.