1492	12	5	These developments are not exclusive ly brought by the\npandemic. It is highly likely that pre-pandemic investments in\nautomation and digitalisation have already prevented a worse\neconomic outcome from the pa ndemic . Since several years,\nautomation technologies have been seen as means to bring back manufacturing to high -cost-countries and counter the\nimpact of retiring experienced employees . Some industries,\nsuch as offshore oil and gas, have already been looking to\nautomation and remote operations to reduce safety risks but\nalso to handle a shortage of qualified workers and the\ncorrespondingly high cost of manned operation ( Casey, 2021 ).	Preamble	101	4	\N	\N	{}	[-0.020102423,-0.01856845,0.093437605,-0.03298759,0.02007783,0.043843966,-0.0012107373,0.041637164,-0.05800187,0.015766477,-0.034678735,0.070438184,0.03949432,-0.018626368,-0.004944124,-0.066685244,0.0048907837,-0.111822635,-0.016084312,-0.043506246,-0.037262544,0.029197415,-0.04723148,-0.019529777,-0.049847387,0.00048203598,0.02727895,-0.062361434,-0.02848315,0.07914188,-0.08232654,0.024609435,-0.010676437,0.006385525,0.03062752,-0.04081402,-0.0053837746,-0.0010362857,0.037885774,-0.078565486,0.027489383,-0.15738608,-0.040950797,-0.018005757,0.06830043,0.011667562,-0.03983689,-0.104350135,-0.03107829,-0.06949285,-0.07090083,-0.03170135,0.04714379,-0.055291895,0.00054145936,-0.033649758,0.04091587,-0.10031436,-0.044803966,0.03238422,-0.0035846466,-0.0046626166,-0.0066978233,-0.0042139487,0.06305386,0.00745471,0.029620374,-0.04608085,-0.0154408,0.036884945,-0.023031076,-0.04897253,-0.024652796,0.04467939,0.0437424,-0.027306927,0.009650011,-0.006285437,0.086487055,-0.031659644,0.080523685,-0.04915264,0.016224198,0.037989438,-0.05820515,0.033636767,-0.0133285485,0.003665548,0.08848572,-0.039521802,-0.047379006,-0.080825396,0.018466573,0.07367126,0.012718456,0.032858998,-0.019039847,0.015417868,-0.014524593,-0.05118287,0.007960157,-0.03532753,0.004521239,-0.028585527,-0.102358386,0.0221061