1519	12	32	The intersection of the trends of reduced availability of labour ,\nincreasing demands for sustainability, and the necessity to\ncombat climate change brings up the possibility of designing a\nnew generation of processes and plants with an embedded Unmanned and Autonomous Systems: Future of Automation in Process and\nEnergy Industries\nFrancesco Borghesan * Marta Zagorowska* Mehmet Mercangöz *\n* Department of Chemical Engineering, Imperial College London ,\nSouth Kensington Campus, London SW7 2AZ, UK (m.mercangoz@imperial.ac.uk )\nAbstract : Process and energy industries have been recognised as adopters of high levels of automation\ncompared to other sectors. Nonetheless, human cognitive input still plays a critical role in the operation of\nprocess plants and replication of these cognitive capabilities remains a key challenge for advancing\nautomation levels. In this paper, w e provide an analysis of process and energy industries based on a scenario\nof reduced availability of skilled labour and increased demands for safety, sustainability, and resilience.	Preamble	156	3	\N	\N	{}	[0.030870542,-0.00704425,-0.02362984,0.011149841,0.02058281,-0.0140223345,0.009570416,0.00527504,-0.03169959,0.06460521,-0.011040601,-0.03606505,0.081178464,0.0028782105,0.011204021,0.018810334,0.012652912,-0.0965634,-0.06953407,-0.08246873,0.049003396,0.006483979,-0.010178287,0.031621974,-0.049120594,0.10031559,-0.0662851,0.03626798,-0.05878111,0.025582213,-0.025958493,0.0049972613,0.05608952,0.00012746567,0.11706916,0.022183508,0.015746599,-0.019360071,0.009645121,-0.11024449,-0.038784977,-0.1459401,0.004937034,-0.031831,-0.035235904,0.085977525,-0.018179616,-0.13746516,0.0010747481,-0.08764217,-0.05224358,-0.010097576,0.05448051,-0.040038574,-0.009150008,-0.0019957914,0.102985,0.006042266,-0.016767068,-0.053385902,0.02002886,-0.04519212,-0.008372194,0.014643257,0.016140943,0.049039617,-0.07025198,0.012032354,-0.019866439,-0.095283635,-0.008207497,-0.026046753,-0.058984604,-0