1537	12	50	Monitoring and inspection of the hardware components\nfor IT and OT systems as well as the electrical infrastructure is carried out by technicians. For maintenance related tasks , the characteri sation of\nequipment condition requires a visual inspection in most cases. Performing maintenance action s and their subsequent\nvalidation relies on human sensing as well . Detecti on of fire or\nenvironmental emergencies is mostly instrumented but if the Core production\nprocess\n(e.g. reactors,\nseparators,\nmachines, mills)Auxiliary systems\n(e.g. power plant,\nsubstation, boilers,\nair compressors,\ncooling water, waste -\nwater)\nAutomation and safety systems\n(e.g. controllers, I/O units, computers, cables, instruments)Terminals, yard,\nwarehouse\n(e.g. storage area,\ntanks, loading\nbays, train tracks,\nports, pipelines)\nPerimeter security\n(e.g. walls, gates, fences, cameras)Information and communication technology systems\n(e.g. computers, routers, cables, satellite dishes, antennas)Environmental\nand fire\nresponse\n(e.g. washers,\nbooms, trucks,\nfire\nextinguishers)\nMechanical\nworkshops\n(e.g. tools,\nworkbenches)Analytical labs\n(e.g. tools,\nbenches,\nanalyzers)\nFig. 1. An overview of the constituents of a generic process\nplant.	876 Francesco Borghesan et al. / IF AC PapersOnLine 55-7 (2022) 875–882	162	5	\N	\N	{}	[-0.08455835,-0.019525796,-0.009471324,-0.06922912,0.0993924,-0.032275934,0.08289726,0.07824603,-0.010197398,0.03430931,-0.007862952,-0.03474937,0.03976619,0.015015749,-0.082510605,-0.048554152,0.049850866,-0.023268586,-0.041988563,-0.07305458,0.011444348,0.03390862,-0.04448377,0.011703384,-0.14807276,0.0026194376,-0.0194649,-0.031141957,-0.015182575,-0.04145455,-0.04017569,0.06433973,0.048579916,0.0064617707,0.06871015,0.083431154,0.07743856,-0.024452366,0.031718574,-0.031580098,-0.026790392,-0.08182233,-0.010207545,-0.0061287372,0.025982857,-0.052764233,-0.021246992,-0.16630621,-0.05928022,-0.027540918,-0.06855992,0.012838826,0.0031