1548	12	61	Monitoring and inspection of the hardware components\nfor IT and OT systems as well as the electrical infrastructure\nis carried out by technicians. For maintenance related tasks , the characteri sation of\nequipment condition requires a visual inspection in most cases. Performing maintenance action s and their subsequent\nvalidation relies on human sensing as well . Detecti on of fire or\nenvironmental emergencies is mostly instrumented but if the Core production\nprocess\n(e.g. reactors,\nseparators,\nmachines, mills)Auxiliary systems\n(e.g. power plant,\nsubstation, boilers,\nair compressors,\ncooling water, waste -\nwater)\nAutomation and safety systems\n(e.g. controllers, I/O units, computers, cables, instruments)Terminals, yard,\nwarehouse\n(e.g. storage area,\ntanks, loading\nbays, train tracks,\nports, pipelines)\nPerimeter security\n(e.g. walls, gates, fences, cameras)Information and communication technology systems\n(e.g. computers, routers, cables, satellite dishes, antennas)Environmental\nand fire\nresponse\n(e.g. washers,\nbooms, trucks,\nfire\nextinguishers)\nMechanical\nworkshops\n(e.g. tools,\nworkbenches)Analytical labs\n(e.g. tools,\nbenches,\nanalyzers)\nFig. 1. An overview of the constituents of a generic process\nplant.	876 Francesco Borghesan et al. / IF AC PapersOnLine 55-7 (2022) 875–882	162	5	\N	\N	{}	[-0.08455837,-0.0195258,-0.009471351,-0.0692291,0.09939244,-0.032275915,0.08289725,0.07824603,-0.010197383,0.034309287,-0.007862954,-0.03474938,0.03976619,0.015015733,-0.0825106,-0.04855414,0.049850866,-0.0232686,-0.041988578,-0.07305456,0.01144437,0.033908647,-0.04448377,0.011703378,-0.14807278,0.0026194588,-0.019464906,-0.031141974,-0.015182561,-0.041454554,-0.040175684,0.06433971,0.04857992,0.0064617703,0.0687102,0.08343115,0.07743855,-0.024452407,0.03171854,-0.031580076,-0.026790403,-0.08182232,-0.010207582,-0.0061287335,0.025982862,-0.052764237,-0.021246979,-0.16630623,-0.059280243,-0.027540928,-0.068559915,0.012838841,0.0031396