1557	12	70	In general, mechanisation of regular operations related manual\nlabour is likely to be feasible in most plants due to the repeated\nand plannable nature of the involved tasks. On the other hand,\nboth operations related tro ubleshooting such as removal of\nclogging objects or handling of a jammed machine and the\nmanual labour associated with maintenance tasks pose more\nserious challenges for direct automation. The troubleshooting\nwork will be difficult to automate due to the h igh variability of\nthe involved sub\n-tasks.	2.2 Future of automation for manual labour and human	83	3	\N	\N	{}	[-0.06467883,0.034812525,-0.014980682,0.046125174,-0.044744913,-0.10508651,0.0047562425,-0.0099568125,-0.13192716,0.03597475,0.017986463,0.042585365,0.013059284,0.05214515,-0.07808101,-0.06168782,-0.0028573219,-0.0398564,-0.05539668,-0.08039446,0.0026188968,0.0043251235,-0.077232145,-0.012760096,-0.035569794,-0.04923834,-0.092291586,0.031012885,0.028588174,-0.073022656,-0.05175901,0.033748027,0.04851448,0.004234385,0.03212533,0.033455577,0.012691803,-0.033919927,0.028054114,-0.016898073,0.032183934,-0.06848565,-0.013946472,0.003892714,-0.020705167,0.06124855,-0.08235223,-0.053477507,-0.012709811,-0.03734745,-0.025606094,0.0015753424,0.098992616,-0.004983464,0.032340154,0.019411717,0.11185916,0.038209002,0.008605159,-0.00088770007,0.015406973,0.018531192,-0.018280752,-0.018320862,0.07826404,-0.055454306,-0.021968532,-0.030875169,0.06715814,0.047194812,0.016167115,-0.049330674,-0.053708557,0.053308986,0.049568508,-0.0052615395,-0.051253777,-0.03022265,-0.045333456,-0.019913202,-0.058429927,-0.0029513328,-0.0201516,0.016968766,-0.03310595,0.029533459,-0.028983533,0.040350694,0.11237933,-0.037874073,0.026542827,-0.04749573,-0.04407205,-0.028765483,0.024915805,0.05209362,0.104636244,0.017238777,-0.06245045,-0.03832966,-0.038778726,-0.022803146,0.047535222,-0.03673051,-0.0030999663,0.037162542,-0.02931304,-0.07776108,-3.6539e-05,-0.07887324,-0.06917942,0.039408308,-0.0006006