1598	12	111	However, in case of partial\nhorizontal autonomy , where some unit operations are\ncontrolled by an au tonomous system and others by human\noperators , the testing process will require the input of human\ndecisions – which could further complicate testing efforts. Most critical decision -making tasks carried ou t by plant\noperators involve the handling of abnormal operations. Often\nsuch decision -making tasks involve discrete actions , such as\nturning machinery on or off, diverting flows , or activating or\ndeactivating control functions .	3.4 Role of plant models for autonomous systems	85	3	\N	\N	{}	[0.005934134,0.00953362,0.009084137,-0.008320404,-0.038401846,-0.09221329,-0.007995557,0.01010761,0.0032797048,0.11791397,0.112564415,-0.0064534415,-0.011185829,0.03711671,-0.014811069,-0.039917782,0.039018907,-0.028123055,-0.09942315,-0.013913889,0.05750123,-0.028310556,-0.0875813,0.019511338,-0.09814282,0.00867753,-0.06788318,-0.031791337,0.06232157,-0.10074342,-0.011032189,0.042754587,0.08893657,-0.021132842,-0.039141197,0.04957283,0.0057296064,-0.08525157,0.009231823,-0.008829309,-0.013223622,-0.1135162,-0.02539007,-0.03095605,-0.029005414,0.045506172,-0.03086064,-0.09469737,-0.005204823,-0.056876313,-0.015000767,0.009537642,0.027272578,-0.048367143,0.0065476517,-0.02122123,0.1304112,0.0074484935,0.040447142,-0.01014201,-0.01724904,-0.01913938,-0.054947957,-0.010943518,0.0549333,0.005522064,-0.08276512,-0.095095664,0.001352944,-0.00077794766,0.027099583,-0.04476745,-0.027524116,-0.014515826,0.047454316,-0.00097581296,-0.014105881,-0.069129355,0.005736703,-0.049014535,0.0017534086,0.039906844,-0.024111778,0.034723483,0.01152648,0.06118345,-0.01549095,0.041477367,0.0725272,-0.008785167,-0.02628396,-0.07348989,0.0038224314,-0.03477388,0.03628707,0.0240798,0.007298899,-0.020406801,-0.056165237,-0.014496473,0.0009893003,-0.06890016,-0.004259451,-0.0005974546,0.006609401,0.019783823,-0.018812517,-0.1536458,0.059566114,-0.081250526,-0.09239203,-0.036133755,-