79396,-0.039017998,0.021364063,0.019890677,0.02359061,0.0855646,-0.0039466745,0.07386654,-0.006014234,0.004273671,-0.0006295216,-0.012926829,-0.073278874,0.03644883,-0.076751545,-2.565144e-08,-0.04380655,0.029789517,0.11081488,0.08080151,0.07428457,0.053789884,-0.05296358,0.057264205,-0.05188583,-0.059952516,0.026696587,-0.054932073,0.08979253,-0.0021338854,0.15757824,0.083705045,-0.04783335,0.071610354,-0.038822956,-0.03950992,0.10619587,0.02569309,-0.07771298,-0.014378999,0.029011091,-0.016376477,-0.03845068,0.07232937,-0.11284981,0.043517187,0.014925587,0.021155212,0.02860202,3.4697896e-05,0.11345804,0.02679427,0.08558862,-0.038178273,-0.027300622,0.015414624,-0.083672084,0.114970505,-0.08080876,0.022048244,0.13961947,-0.03097146,0.014303187,-0.033097927,-0.0074062417,-0.05156961,0.023792,-0.018210016,-0.044548444,0.07364844,0.0575702,0.006702009,-0.019771151,-0.04248833,-0.039496504,0.106905185,0.098447874,0.04438717,-0.03706147,-0.04843581]	{5,6,5,5,6}	{483,686,581,489,767}	2	5	{0.609,0.588,0.567,0.538,0.537}	0.568	gemini-3-flash-preview	\N	Based on the provided documents, human performance can degrade when collaborating with AI due to a lack of proper trust calibration, often manifesting as over-reliance or automation bias.\n\n### How Performance Degrades Due to Over-confidence in AI\nWhen humans place excessive trust in AI outputs—a phenomenon known as **over-trust** or **automation bias**—they may unquestioningly accept AI suggestions even when those suggestions are incorrect [Source 1, Source 4]. This leads to several performance issues:\n\n*   **The "Performance Paradox":** Research indicates that human-AI teams often perform worse than the AI system acting alone [Source 1, Source 2]. This happens because humans fail to exercise their own judgment to override AI errors.\n*   **System 1 Thinking:** Over-reliance is often linked to the dual-process theory of cognition. Users may rely on "System 1" (fast, intuitive) thinking rather than "System 2" (slow, deliberative) thinking, especially when faced with complex tasks or explanations that trigger cognitive overload [Source 4].\n*   **High-Stakes Risks:** In domains like healthcare, over-reliance can lead to harmful or incorrect recommendations that have immediate and significant consequences for safety and health outcomes [Source 4].\n\n### Proposed Ways to Integrate AI Without Performance Degradation\nTo prevent this degradation, researchers suggest various strategies for **reliance calibration**, which aims to help users follow AI when it is correct and disregard it when it is wrong.\n\n*   **Reflective AI-Driven Questions:** Implementing reflective questions within the interface can prompt users to think more critically about the AI's reasoning. This encourages users to engage more deeply ("System 2" thinking) and has been shown to significantly improve reliance calibration [Source 3].\n*   **Visual Presentation Techniques:** Using simple visual highlights rather than just written text or raw predictions can reduce over-reliance during difficult tasks [Source 5].\n*   **Example-Based Presentations:** Providing examples alongside AI outputs can offer stronger signals of the AI’s potential unreliability, preventing the "blind acceptance" of incorrect recommendations [Source 5].\n*   **Balancing Cognitive Load:** While engagement is necessary, designers must ensure that the interface does not become so complex that it introduces excessive cognitive load, which can lead to overthinking or a complete loss of trust (under-reliance) [Source 3].\n*   **Trust Calibration Strategies:** Effective integration requires a balance between trust and skepticism. Strategies that emphasize "trust calibration" seek to move beyond simply providing explanations (XAI), which alone have not consistently mitigated trust issues [Source 4].\n\n**Sources:**\n*   [Source 1] Engaging With AI: How Interface Design Shapes Human-AI Collaboration in High-Stakes Decision Making (Preamble)\n*   [Source 2] Enhancing Intuitive Decision-Making and Reliance Through Human–AI Collaboration: A Review (Introduction)\n*   [Source 3] Engaging With AI: How Interface Design Shapes Human-AI Collaboration in High-Stakes Decision Making (Section 3.2)\n*   [Source 4] Engaging With AI: How Interface Design Shapes Human-AI Collaboration in High-Stakes Decision Making (Section AIAI)\n*   [Source 5] Enhancing Intuitive Decision-Making and Reliance Through Human–AI Collaboration: A Review (Section 3)	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2025-12-22 14:10:25.443088	\N
